1
00:01:28,856 --> 00:01:29,889
So refreshing.

2
00:01:29,890 --> 00:01:31,492
(Bukit Lawang, Indonesia)

3
00:01:32,359 --> 00:01:33,893
The grass is longer here.

4
00:01:35,562 --> 00:01:38,063
We're getting deeper into the jungle.

5
00:01:38,064 --> 00:01:39,231
The grass is longer.

6
00:01:39,232 --> 00:01:40,666
I see something...

7
00:01:40,667 --> 00:01:42,935
that looks like a fern
from the Paleozoic era.

8
00:01:43,504 --> 00:01:44,404
Like this.

9
00:01:45,172 --> 00:01:46,004
You're right.

10
00:01:46,005 --> 00:01:46,939
(They see unfamiliar plants.)

11
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:50,176
Ipu, I want to see that grass.

12
00:01:50,377 --> 00:01:51,911
When we touch it...

13
00:01:52,989 --> 00:01:54,756
When we touch it, it curls up.

14
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:55,948
It's not here.

15
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:56,915
Not here?

16
00:01:56,916 --> 00:01:58,785
- Maybe we can look over there.
- Is that so?

17
00:01:58,786 --> 00:02:00,219
We have it in Korea.

18
00:02:01,622 --> 00:02:02,722
They don't have it here.

19
00:02:03,457 --> 00:02:04,958
Maybe they haven't found it.

20
00:02:04,959 --> 00:02:06,059
There's no way it doesn't grow here.

21
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:08,895
- One minute, please.
- Okay.

22
00:02:08,896 --> 00:02:09,796
One minute?

23
00:02:09,930 --> 00:02:10,697
- Are we done?
- Why?

24
00:02:10,698 --> 00:02:12,799
- Is he going home?
- Let me pick some of those leaves.

25
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,434
He's going to pick that.

26
00:02:14,668 --> 00:02:15,735
- What's that?
- Amazing.

27
00:02:15,869 --> 00:02:17,436
Is he going to climb that tree?

28
00:02:17,614 --> 00:02:19,415
Is he going to shake that tree
and knock something down?

29
00:02:19,453 --> 00:02:20,240
(Jumping)

30
00:02:20,808 --> 00:02:22,109
(Ipu climbs the tree.)

31
00:02:22,110 --> 00:02:23,510
He's like Tarzan.

32
00:02:23,511 --> 00:02:24,744
That's really cool.

33
00:02:24,745 --> 00:02:26,246
- Seriously.
- That's awesome.

34
00:02:27,414 --> 00:02:28,547
That's the way to live.

35
00:02:29,450 --> 00:02:31,651
(Watching in awe)

36
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:37,557
(Skillfully picking a leaf)

37
00:02:38,258 --> 00:02:40,960
You can tell that he loves this job.

38
00:02:40,961 --> 00:02:41,894
That's really cool.

39
00:02:41,895 --> 00:02:43,362
He probably doesn't see it as work.

40
00:02:43,897 --> 00:02:45,464
It's like introducing your home.

41
00:02:45,599 --> 00:02:46,665
A room tour.

42
00:02:46,666 --> 00:02:47,833
He's giving us a room tour.

43
00:02:48,235 --> 00:02:50,236
He took us on a room tour.

44
00:02:50,237 --> 00:02:51,437
Ipu's room tour.

45
00:02:52,206 --> 00:02:53,406
Do you know what this is for?

46
00:02:54,641 --> 00:02:56,208
- Do you know?
- Is that sugarcane?

47
00:02:56,378 --> 00:02:57,242
No.

48
00:02:57,544 --> 00:02:58,911
- What is that?
- This can be used as a dye.

49
00:02:58,912 --> 00:02:59,945
Smooth?

50
00:02:59,946 --> 00:03:01,914
- Smooth?
- For painting?

51
00:03:02,716 --> 00:03:03,949
You can dye things with this.

52
00:03:04,785 --> 00:03:06,453
(They finally understand.)

53
00:03:06,454 --> 00:03:07,854
Can I touch it?

54
00:03:07,988 --> 00:03:09,555
- Maybe put it here.
- Okay.

55
00:03:09,957 --> 00:03:10,857
Maybe here.

56
00:03:11,058 --> 00:03:13,760
(Rubbing it on a white cloth)

57
00:03:15,162 --> 00:03:17,964
(It dyes the cloth red!)

58
00:03:18,365 --> 00:03:19,999
Is it some kind of pigment?

59
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,734
A natural dye!

60
00:03:22,469 --> 00:03:25,604
(The more he rubs it,
the darker the color gets.)

61
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,340
It will stay until you get back to Korea.

62
00:03:28,776 --> 00:03:30,176
Yes, I'm serious.

63
00:03:30,310 --> 00:03:31,577
(The color holds up well!)

64
00:03:31,578 --> 00:03:32,578
That's okay.

65
00:03:32,679 --> 00:03:34,647
- Do you have another?
- Just one color?

66
00:03:34,648 --> 00:03:35,547
One color.

67
00:03:36,083 --> 00:03:37,350
That's so interesting.

68
00:03:37,651 --> 00:03:39,619
It's like a colored pencil.

69
00:03:39,788 --> 00:03:41,554
That's fascinating.

70
00:03:41,555 --> 00:03:42,855
It's so much fun.

71
00:03:42,856 --> 00:03:44,423
This room tour is fun.

72
00:03:44,424 --> 00:03:46,158
- It's like a jungle adventure.
- I know.

73
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:47,727
This is not bad.

74
00:03:47,728 --> 00:03:48,894
It's pretty good so far.

75
00:03:48,895 --> 00:03:50,896
It's like a trekking route.

76
00:03:51,198 --> 00:03:52,465
If we keep going,

77
00:03:52,699 --> 00:03:54,333
- we'll see monkeys...
- Yes.

78
00:03:54,334 --> 00:03:56,736
- and orangutans too, right?
- I think so.

79
00:03:56,737 --> 00:03:59,338
The way to our lodging goes
through where orangutans live.

80
00:04:00,908 --> 00:04:02,075
Here?

81
00:04:02,076 --> 00:04:04,777
We're visiting the orangutans' home, then.

82
00:04:05,512 --> 00:04:07,679
There isn't a designated area
where they live.

83
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:10,049
No. They just roam freely in the wild.

84
00:04:10,050 --> 00:04:11,978
We can see them on our way to our place.

85
00:04:11,979 --> 00:04:13,232
(The whole jungle is their home.)

86
00:04:13,821 --> 00:04:15,221
It feels like this is
where the jungle starts.

87
00:04:15,222 --> 00:04:17,456
I think we're entering the national park.

88
00:04:17,457 --> 00:04:19,391
(Arriving at the entrance
of the national park)

89
00:04:19,593 --> 00:04:21,360
Let's start trekking now.

90
00:04:21,796 --> 00:04:23,162
Okay, trekking!

91
00:04:23,163 --> 00:04:24,063
Let's go inside.

92
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:28,334
It's getting started.

93
00:04:28,335 --> 00:04:30,136
That was just the intro so far.

94
00:04:30,137 --> 00:04:32,572
Let's look for orangutans and monkeys.

95
00:04:32,573 --> 00:04:34,707
- Okay!
- Okay!

96
00:04:34,975 --> 00:04:36,609
Let's just do it!

97
00:04:37,010 --> 00:04:38,410
Let's go.

98
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:41,548
I'm walking in lunges,
squeezing my glutes.

99
00:04:41,915 --> 00:04:43,515
It's a little muddy here.

100
00:04:43,917 --> 00:04:46,886
We're pretty used to mud now.

101
00:04:46,887 --> 00:04:47,753
Right.

102
00:04:47,888 --> 00:04:50,089
The elephant hotel was muddy too.

103
00:04:50,557 --> 00:04:52,525
We're very familiar with Mr. Mud now.

104
00:04:54,595 --> 00:04:56,062
- Mr. Mud?
- Yes.

105
00:04:56,330 --> 00:04:57,563
Mr. Mud,

106
00:04:58,465 --> 00:04:59,598
let's break up.

107
00:05:02,002 --> 00:05:04,002
(A random skit)

108
00:05:04,003 --> 00:05:05,071
I'm speechless.

109
00:05:06,874 --> 00:05:08,007
Mr. Mud.

110
00:05:08,642 --> 00:05:10,676
Mr. Mud, let's break up.

111
00:05:11,545 --> 00:05:12,845
Mr. Mud, I'm going to study abroad.

112
00:05:13,247 --> 00:05:14,681
Stop following me.

113
00:05:14,682 --> 00:05:15,815
(Don't look for me.)

114
00:05:16,250 --> 00:05:18,218
(Who are you?)

115
00:05:18,219 --> 00:05:19,052
That's so funny.

116
00:05:19,887 --> 00:05:21,054
Number Three seems to be struggling.

117
00:05:21,055 --> 00:05:22,689
No, I'm good.

118
00:05:22,690 --> 00:05:25,225
You look so tired from behind.

119
00:05:25,226 --> 00:05:26,960
(She looks exhausted from behind.)

120
00:05:27,071 --> 00:05:28,771
Number Three, are you okay?

121
00:05:29,663 --> 00:05:30,930
Number Three isn't tired.

122
00:05:30,931 --> 00:05:32,465
(The company commander is
disappointed in Number Three.)

123
00:05:32,634 --> 00:05:34,233
I'm so glad...

124
00:05:34,535 --> 00:05:35,768
that it's not blazing hot.

125
00:05:35,769 --> 00:05:36,636
I agree.

126
00:05:37,538 --> 00:05:39,839
If it was scorching hot,

127
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,241
- I would've run away.
- I know.

128
00:05:41,642 --> 00:05:42,742
It's a real jungle.

129
00:05:43,911 --> 00:05:45,211
(The slope gets steeper.)

130
00:05:45,212 --> 00:05:47,180
Now it's uphill.

131
00:05:47,908 --> 00:05:49,909
(Calling Ipu)

132
00:05:50,117 --> 00:05:53,419
When did you start climbing trees?

133
00:05:53,854 --> 00:05:56,689
Do you want to try?

134
00:05:57,191 --> 00:05:58,291
No.

135
00:05:58,292 --> 00:05:59,259
That's not what she meant.

136
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:01,260
Goodness.

137
00:06:01,795 --> 00:06:03,162
Is he going to show us?

138
00:06:03,163 --> 00:06:04,029
Here.

139
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:05,097
He's telling me to try.

140
00:06:05,098 --> 00:06:06,931
(Pushing through the grass,
straight to a tree)

141
00:06:08,869 --> 00:06:11,337
- Let's try it.
- I want to try climbing it.

142
00:06:11,338 --> 00:06:12,672
- You might be good at it.
- I think so too.

143
00:06:12,673 --> 00:06:13,673
You might be good.

144
00:06:14,708 --> 00:06:15,741
(The expert shows an example.)

145
00:06:15,742 --> 00:06:16,676
That looks like fun.

146
00:06:18,045 --> 00:06:19,445
I've always wanted to climb a tree.

147
00:06:19,446 --> 00:06:20,680
- Let's try it.
- Okay.

148
00:06:20,681 --> 00:06:22,615
(Climbing the tree with bare hands)

149
00:06:23,450 --> 00:06:25,485
Let's go!

150
00:06:25,486 --> 00:06:26,552
Come up.

151
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:27,620
(He reached the top quickly.)

152
00:06:28,388 --> 00:06:29,254
Me too.

153
00:06:29,255 --> 00:06:31,991
Isn't there a limit
to how many people can climb the tree?

154
00:06:33,927 --> 00:06:34,860
- Amazing!
- How is it?

155
00:06:35,562 --> 00:06:36,829
You're climbing well.

156
00:06:36,830 --> 00:06:37,763
It's fun.

157
00:06:37,764 --> 00:06:39,365
How far up did he climb?

158
00:06:39,633 --> 00:06:41,167
(Relaxed)

159
00:06:43,136 --> 00:06:44,403
She's so good at climbing.

160
00:06:45,806 --> 00:06:48,074
(She's already halfway up.)

161
00:06:48,075 --> 00:06:49,409
- This is crazy.
- She's a monkey.

162
00:06:49,876 --> 00:06:52,344
I'm so talented, right?

163
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:53,916
Be careful.

164
00:06:53,917 --> 00:06:56,348
(She's talented in many ways.)

165
00:06:56,349 --> 00:06:57,483
Let's go!

166
00:06:57,684 --> 00:06:58,851
She's good at it.

167
00:07:00,654 --> 00:07:02,588
(Singing)

168
00:07:03,309 --> 00:07:08,294
(She's talented like a monkey.)

169
00:07:08,762 --> 00:07:10,630
(She can dance while climbing a tree.)

170
00:07:10,631 --> 00:07:11,897
Am I impressive?

171
00:07:13,066 --> 00:07:14,333
I'll go down.

172
00:07:16,203 --> 00:07:17,503
My lower body is so weak.

173
00:07:18,638 --> 00:07:21,340
(Sian gave up while flailing around.)

174
00:07:22,042 --> 00:07:23,376
Are you going to go down that way?

175
00:07:23,377 --> 00:07:24,944
(Pulling)

176
00:07:25,345 --> 00:07:26,211
Really?

177
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:31,583
(Tarzan)

178
00:07:31,985 --> 00:07:33,118
That's cool.

179
00:07:34,621 --> 00:07:36,188
This is his playground.

180
00:07:36,757 --> 00:07:38,157
That's impressive.

181
00:07:38,158 --> 00:07:40,459
(He's basically one with the tree.)

182
00:07:40,661 --> 00:07:41,894
Will Harimu do that too?

183
00:07:41,895 --> 00:07:44,063
She should just come down, just in case.

184
00:07:44,064 --> 00:07:44,930
- Right.
- I'm scared for her.

185
00:07:45,299 --> 00:07:46,065
Okay.

186
00:07:46,066 --> 00:07:47,066
(One step down)

187
00:07:47,091 --> 00:07:48,692
She's using her arms to climb down.

188
00:07:50,270 --> 00:07:52,137
(Turning)

189
00:07:52,138 --> 00:07:53,072
Watch out.

190
00:07:53,740 --> 00:07:55,708
- Did you get any splinters?
- I'm good.

191
00:07:55,709 --> 00:07:57,609
That was fun, like pole dancing.

192
00:07:57,634 --> 00:07:58,735
Okay!

193
00:07:59,146 --> 00:08:00,480
- Okay!
- Okay!

194
00:08:00,481 --> 00:08:01,981
I shouldn't have done that.

195
00:08:01,982 --> 00:08:02,983
My shoulder hurts.

196
00:08:02,984 --> 00:08:03,783
It hurts?

197
00:08:03,784 --> 00:08:04,751
I feel like it got a little twisted.

198
00:08:04,752 --> 00:08:06,719
- She did her best,
- I couldn't do it.

199
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:08,888
but the talented one got
all our attention.

200
00:08:09,489 --> 00:08:10,622
She didn't get enough attention.

201
00:08:10,623 --> 00:08:11,757
I'm so talented, right?

202
00:08:11,758 --> 00:08:13,325
She got the spotlight,

203
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:15,494
- Right.
- so I gave up and came down.

204
00:08:15,495 --> 00:08:16,528
She did too well.

205
00:08:16,529 --> 00:08:18,764
She totally stole the spotlight.

206
00:08:18,932 --> 00:08:20,065
Jane!

207
00:08:20,534 --> 00:08:21,834
Jane from "Tarzan."

208
00:08:23,503 --> 00:08:25,871
Is he talking about Jane from "Tarzan?"

209
00:08:25,872 --> 00:08:27,539
"Tarzan."

210
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:29,975
I think he liked it.

211
00:08:31,445 --> 00:08:33,480
No, I'm a city girl.

212
00:08:35,849 --> 00:08:37,983
(Getting ahead of herself)

213
00:08:38,051 --> 00:08:39,118
City girls!

214
00:08:39,119 --> 00:08:43,656
(The city girls' jungle trip continues.)

215
00:08:43,657 --> 00:08:44,657
By the way,

216
00:08:45,158 --> 00:08:46,728
I bet it feels so cool in the valley.

217
00:08:46,729 --> 00:08:48,194
- Seriously.
- Right?

218
00:08:48,195 --> 00:08:49,761
- I'd jump in.
- We don't even need bathing suits.

219
00:08:49,762 --> 00:08:50,863
We should jump right in.

220
00:08:50,864 --> 00:08:51,765
Right in the water.

221
00:08:52,132 --> 00:08:54,700
I'm so happy
I haven't gotten any mosquito bites.

222
00:08:54,701 --> 00:08:56,034
There's no sun either.

223
00:08:56,035 --> 00:08:57,169
(Jungle life is going pretty well.)

224
00:08:57,230 --> 00:08:58,564
Do you want to try sitting here?

225
00:08:58,786 --> 00:09:00,272
Climbing this tree?

226
00:09:00,273 --> 00:09:01,840
- A swing?
- That looks like a swing.

227
00:09:02,109 --> 00:09:03,376
A swing?

228
00:09:03,377 --> 00:09:05,678
(The tree branch is hanging down
like a swing.)

229
00:09:05,679 --> 00:09:06,612
It's like a swing.

230
00:09:06,613 --> 00:09:07,980
How did the tree grow like this?

231
00:09:08,749 --> 00:09:10,049
A natural swing.

232
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:11,316
Won Ji.

233
00:09:11,418 --> 00:09:12,385
Won Ji.

234
00:09:12,386 --> 00:09:14,086
- Won Ji.
- Grab that.

235
00:09:14,888 --> 00:09:15,788
Wait.

236
00:09:15,789 --> 00:09:17,690
It's getting interesting again.

237
00:09:17,691 --> 00:09:19,258
No, I'll sit like a deity.

238
00:09:19,946 --> 00:09:21,613
Like the queen of this jungle.

239
00:09:22,229 --> 00:09:23,429
Okay!

240
00:09:23,430 --> 00:09:25,131
(Shutting her eyes tightly)

241
00:09:25,165 --> 00:09:26,098
Wait.

242
00:09:26,266 --> 00:09:28,300
- Wait.
- Wait.

243
00:09:28,301 --> 00:09:30,135
(Even Ipu realizes she's a scaredy-cat.)

244
00:09:30,136 --> 00:09:31,003
Harimu, try it.

245
00:09:32,706 --> 00:09:33,706
(Gasping)

246
00:09:33,707 --> 00:09:34,907
What did you just do?

247
00:09:35,743 --> 00:09:36,609
What's with me?

248
00:09:36,610 --> 00:09:37,877
(Curled up)

249
00:09:37,878 --> 00:09:39,278
Have fun, girl!

250
00:09:40,347 --> 00:09:41,213
I look like...

251
00:09:41,681 --> 00:09:42,948
I'm pooping.

252
00:09:45,285 --> 00:09:47,019
- Okay!
- Okay!

253
00:09:47,020 --> 00:09:48,120
(Won Ji's turn)

254
00:09:48,555 --> 00:09:50,990
Lift your feet. There you go!

255
00:09:50,991 --> 00:09:52,858
Her belly is shaking.

256
00:09:53,126 --> 00:09:55,160
Won Ji, engage your core.

257
00:09:55,161 --> 00:09:58,097
(Who made her shake?)

258
00:09:58,098 --> 00:09:59,064
That's good.

259
00:09:59,065 --> 00:10:01,867
(Ipu shows off an advanced skill.)

260
00:10:01,868 --> 00:10:04,536
- I want to try that too.
- Try it!

261
00:10:04,537 --> 00:10:06,538
- I want to try that.
- Show me what you've got!

262
00:10:06,539 --> 00:10:09,007
Make it, make it hot!
Show me what you've got!

263
00:10:09,008 --> 00:10:09,908
(It's Gabee's turn.)

264
00:10:09,909 --> 00:10:11,043
This might be really hard.

265
00:10:11,044 --> 00:10:13,178
- Put your leg up there.
- Here?

266
00:10:13,413 --> 00:10:14,313
I'll push it.

267
00:10:14,314 --> 00:10:16,181
(Hanging)

268
00:10:23,142 --> 00:10:25,057
You're doing well! There you go!

269
00:10:25,325 --> 00:10:26,138
You're the best!

270
00:10:29,062 --> 00:10:30,796
(Screaming)

271
00:10:31,565 --> 00:10:33,065
We're in the jungle!

272
00:10:33,567 --> 00:10:35,101
(Showing all her pearly whites)

273
00:10:36,269 --> 00:10:37,303
(Gabee, way to go!)

274
00:10:37,304 --> 00:10:38,271
This is fun.

275
00:10:38,272 --> 00:10:39,906
- It's fun.
- It's so much fun.

276
00:10:39,907 --> 00:10:41,274
- It's really fun.
- Thank you.

277
00:10:41,275 --> 00:10:43,843
There are some activities here and there.

278
00:10:44,678 --> 00:10:46,178
Now let's find some orangutans.

279
00:10:46,179 --> 00:10:47,113
- Okay.
- Okay.

280
00:10:47,114 --> 00:10:48,715
Let's focus and find the orangutans now.

281
00:10:48,740 --> 00:10:50,974
- Orangutans.
- Let's find the orangutans.

282
00:10:51,251 --> 00:10:54,220
There's plenty of fun stuff to do...

283
00:10:54,221 --> 00:10:55,088
besides looking for orangutans.

284
00:10:55,089 --> 00:10:57,489
His "What's in My Room" is so much fun.

285
00:10:57,858 --> 00:10:59,425
- "What's in My Room."
- "What's in My Room."

286
00:10:59,759 --> 00:11:01,927
- "What's in My Room."
- He has so much fun stuff in his room.

287
00:11:01,928 --> 00:11:03,362
Ipu's house tour.

288
00:11:03,363 --> 00:11:04,896
His house tour is so much fun.

289
00:11:05,365 --> 00:11:07,232
(Deeper into the rainforest)

290
00:11:07,233 --> 00:11:08,367
It's refreshing.

291
00:11:08,768 --> 00:11:09,702
The shade.

292
00:11:10,924 --> 00:11:13,859
(Stepping over a fallen tree)

293
00:11:14,441 --> 00:11:15,975
(Dodging all the vines
as they go deeper into the jungle)

294
00:11:15,976 --> 00:11:17,944
It's getting rougher and rougher.

295
00:11:18,713 --> 00:11:20,579
This is nothing like a regular hike.

296
00:11:20,580 --> 00:11:21,614
We keep having...

297
00:11:21,982 --> 00:11:23,749
- to step over trees.
- Right.

298
00:11:24,084 --> 00:11:26,118
This feels like a real jungle.

299
00:11:28,522 --> 00:11:29,588
This is great.

300
00:11:29,589 --> 00:11:30,210
Look.

301
00:11:30,611 --> 00:11:31,812
He's showing us something new.

302
00:11:31,813 --> 00:11:34,114
- Ipu's not even out of breath.
- A room tour.

303
00:11:34,115 --> 00:11:35,649
Ipu is a walking encyclopedia.

304
00:11:37,818 --> 00:11:38,560
(Orangutan call)

305
00:11:39,253 --> 00:11:39,846
(Surprised)

306
00:11:40,253 --> 00:11:41,655
- What?
- He found something.

307
00:11:42,533 --> 00:11:43,691
He must've found a monkey.

308
00:11:44,020 --> 00:11:45,040
- What?
- What?

309
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:46,074
Isn't he calling them?

310
00:11:46,239 --> 00:11:47,880
It's an orangutan nest.

311
00:11:47,881 --> 00:11:48,743
Really?

312
00:11:48,786 --> 00:11:50,445
- Where?
- There.

313
00:11:50,845 --> 00:11:52,414
- There?
- There it is.

314
00:11:52,539 --> 00:11:53,815
- That dark thing.
- Where?

315
00:11:54,716 --> 00:11:55,672
It's pretty high up.

316
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:57,825
I only see the nest, not the orangutan.

317
00:11:57,999 --> 00:11:58,753
(Orangutan call)

318
00:11:59,788 --> 00:12:00,555
(Mimics the call)

319
00:12:01,299 --> 00:12:02,123
(Mimics the call)

320
00:12:02,824 --> 00:12:03,558
(Mimics the call)

321
00:12:04,059 --> 00:12:06,861
Can you see it? You know which one, right?
It's that dark thing.

322
00:12:07,146 --> 00:12:08,263
We'll see one soon.

323
00:12:08,406 --> 00:12:10,532
The monkey builds a nest.

324
00:12:10,533 --> 00:12:11,366
So cute.

325
00:12:11,419 --> 00:12:12,767
I can't wait to see an orangutan.

326
00:12:13,726 --> 00:12:14,569
Cute little orangutan.

327
00:12:15,133 --> 00:12:19,441
Will Mr. Orangutan stay up in the trees?

328
00:12:20,341 --> 00:12:22,811
They're mostly in the trees,
but they come down too.

329
00:12:24,332 --> 00:12:26,047
We should watch the trees closely.

330
00:12:26,414 --> 00:12:28,483
I'll look up as we walk now.

331
00:12:29,884 --> 00:12:31,252
So smart.

332
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:33,288
Brainy, so brainy. Really brainy.

333
00:12:33,289 --> 00:12:35,223
A brainy orangutan.

334
00:12:36,896 --> 00:12:41,450
(Deeper into the mountain forest)

335
00:12:42,996 --> 00:12:43,732
(Orangutan call)

336
00:12:43,770 --> 00:12:45,900
(Repeated orangutan calls)

337
00:12:46,541 --> 00:12:48,801
(Sian slips in an impersonation.)

338
00:12:48,841 --> 00:12:50,739
- Nice.
- That sounded like an orangutan.

339
00:12:50,854 --> 00:12:52,640
You're good at impressions.

340
00:12:53,654 --> 00:12:56,010
(Confident, she makes more ape calls.)

341
00:12:57,545 --> 00:12:59,647
- It's not easy.
- What do you mean, maybe not?

342
00:12:59,648 --> 00:13:01,239
(Maybe not)

343
00:13:02,417 --> 00:13:04,452
- He must've found something else.
- Why are we stopping?

344
00:13:04,632 --> 00:13:07,285
(Ipu suddenly stops.)

345
00:13:07,765 --> 00:13:09,898
I saw a mother orangutan and her baby.

346
00:13:09,899 --> 00:13:13,365
(Are they finally meeting an orangutan?)

347
00:13:13,412 --> 00:13:14,529
(Really?)

348
00:13:15,497 --> 00:13:16,631
He is serious.

349
00:13:16,632 --> 00:13:17,979
(Determined)

350
00:13:18,006 --> 00:13:20,135
Let's follow Ipu.

351
00:13:23,705 --> 00:13:25,306
It's completely muddy.

352
00:13:25,707 --> 00:13:27,707
It's getting more like a jungle.

353
00:13:28,690 --> 00:13:29,784
(Looking around)

354
00:13:30,124 --> 00:13:32,004
(Looking around)

355
00:13:32,450 --> 00:13:36,344
(There's an orangutan somewhere nearby.)

356
00:13:38,915 --> 00:13:41,790
Our Tarzan has stopped.

357
00:13:41,828 --> 00:13:42,757
My gosh.

358
00:13:43,518 --> 00:13:45,292
(Shushing)

359
00:13:45,888 --> 00:13:48,315
(Startled)

360
00:13:48,462 --> 00:13:49,631
There's an orangutan nearby.

361
00:13:49,632 --> 00:13:51,588
(Is it nearby?)

362
00:13:52,142 --> 00:13:53,762
(Over there)

363
00:13:54,255 --> 00:13:58,214
(They quietly begin the pursuit.)

364
00:13:59,894 --> 00:14:01,910
I think I hear something.

365
00:14:02,701 --> 00:14:04,512
Slowly.

366
00:14:06,321 --> 00:14:11,692
(Carefully, one step at a time)

367
00:14:13,188 --> 00:14:14,856
That's the person we saw earlier.

368
00:14:15,452 --> 00:14:17,938
(Startled)

369
00:14:18,305 --> 00:14:19,627
I'm sorry.

370
00:14:20,438 --> 00:14:21,329
Hello.

371
00:14:21,698 --> 00:14:24,677
(So happy to see the safety officer
from the entrance)

372
00:14:24,678 --> 00:14:26,637
(I can't with you.)

373
00:14:26,690 --> 00:14:28,102
He told us to be quiet.

374
00:14:28,703 --> 00:14:30,872
We're being quiet now.

375
00:14:32,750 --> 00:14:33,675
Sorry.

376
00:14:34,250 --> 00:14:35,276
I'm bad at reading the room.

377
00:14:36,644 --> 00:14:40,682
I feel like they'll be with us
until tomorrow.

378
00:14:40,949 --> 00:14:44,953
I saw him behind us,
but he keeps appearing ahead.

379
00:14:46,035 --> 00:14:47,956
It's wild. We keep running into him.

380
00:14:47,957 --> 00:14:49,859
(They resume their trek.)

381
00:14:51,299 --> 00:14:53,659
(Ipu suddenly seems to be in a hurry.)

382
00:14:55,719 --> 00:14:56,865
There must be one.

383
00:14:58,266 --> 00:14:59,834
No way.

384
00:14:59,946 --> 00:15:01,236
It's there.

385
00:15:01,536 --> 00:15:03,071
No, it's there. Over there.

386
00:15:03,226 --> 00:15:04,719
It's right there.

387
00:15:05,979 --> 00:15:08,313
(A glimpse of brown)

388
00:15:08,519 --> 00:15:09,677
Where?

389
00:15:09,866 --> 00:15:11,246
- We can go.
- He says to go.

390
00:15:11,273 --> 00:15:12,347
(Beckoning them over)

391
00:15:12,614 --> 00:15:14,249
Let's go.

392
00:15:14,833 --> 00:15:15,683
Let's go.

393
00:15:16,584 --> 00:15:18,987
They're easier to see than I expected.

394
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:22,394
(Slowly moving higher)

395
00:15:24,867 --> 00:15:26,961
We're really close now.

396
00:15:27,812 --> 00:15:28,897
Here.

397
00:15:29,438 --> 00:15:30,231
Where?

398
00:15:30,385 --> 00:15:32,385
- Here.
- Is it there?

399
00:15:32,386 --> 00:15:34,839
(Thick fur visible through the trees)

400
00:15:34,906 --> 00:15:35,837
There it is.

401
00:15:35,999 --> 00:15:36,838
Amazing!

402
00:15:37,438 --> 00:15:39,007
This is incredible.

403
00:15:39,393 --> 00:15:41,175
- This is amazing.
- Totally.

404
00:15:41,466 --> 00:15:42,343
Let's go.

405
00:15:42,344 --> 00:15:44,738
(They decide to move closer.)

406
00:15:48,249 --> 00:15:50,251
There are two of them.

407
00:15:52,353 --> 00:15:54,381
- Two?
- There are two.

408
00:15:54,807 --> 00:15:55,990
They're so cute.

409
00:15:55,991 --> 00:15:57,325
Are they mother and baby?

410
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:08,029
(At last, their first orangutan encounter)

411
00:16:10,956 --> 00:16:12,763
- A baby.
- A baby.

412
00:16:13,063 --> 00:16:14,242
A baby and its mother.

413
00:16:14,329 --> 00:16:15,710
A mother and baby.

414
00:16:17,412 --> 00:16:18,379
So cute.

415
00:16:18,727 --> 00:16:19,580
So cute.

416
00:16:19,581 --> 00:16:22,087
(A baby orangutan with its mother)

417
00:16:24,527 --> 00:16:25,987
- So cute.
- Hello.

418
00:16:25,988 --> 00:16:27,074
(Flailing)

419
00:16:27,967 --> 00:16:29,541
(Dangling)

420
00:16:29,581 --> 00:16:30,825
- Hey there.
- Hi!

421
00:16:32,961 --> 00:16:35,330
Its messy hair is just my style.

422
00:16:36,386 --> 00:16:37,231
So cute.

423
00:16:37,598 --> 00:16:40,368
This is incredible. I never thought
we'd see one this close.

424
00:16:40,369 --> 00:16:42,932
(Its charmingly messy hair)

425
00:16:42,986 --> 00:16:43,938
Hello.

426
00:16:44,052 --> 00:16:46,174
So cute.
It seems to be saying hello to me.

427
00:16:48,532 --> 00:16:49,510
It's peeing.

428
00:16:49,732 --> 00:16:50,712
(Trickling)

429
00:16:51,266 --> 00:16:52,613
It seems to be saying hello.

430
00:16:53,226 --> 00:16:54,082
Hello.

431
00:16:54,083 --> 00:16:56,486
(Peeing instead of saying hello)

432
00:16:56,818 --> 00:16:58,466
There's a baby too.

433
00:16:58,467 --> 00:17:01,026
(A fascinating sight)

434
00:17:01,087 --> 00:17:02,323
Where did the big one go?

435
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:04,392
It climbed higher.

436
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:06,227
It's avoiding us.

437
00:17:07,095 --> 00:17:09,095
I think it avoids us because we're human.

438
00:17:09,226 --> 00:17:10,465
This is fascinating.

439
00:17:14,066 --> 00:17:15,320
(Scratching)

440
00:17:15,346 --> 00:17:16,204
It's scratching.

441
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,573
Scratch, scratch.

442
00:17:19,546 --> 00:17:21,142
Its hands are really big.

443
00:17:23,226 --> 00:17:24,846
Its hands are huge.

444
00:17:25,786 --> 00:17:27,382
I can't take my eyes off it.

445
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:28,483
It pooped.

446
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:29,517
Poop?

447
00:17:29,953 --> 00:17:30,918
It pooped.

448
00:17:31,245 --> 00:17:32,186
The baby pooped.

449
00:17:32,187 --> 00:17:33,421
Again. Look.

450
00:17:33,473 --> 00:17:34,922
(Plopping)

451
00:17:35,073 --> 00:17:36,891
- Its poop is green.
- You're right.

452
00:17:37,006 --> 00:17:37,892
Is that pee?

453
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,994
Or maybe it's dropping fruit.

454
00:17:39,995 --> 00:17:40,962
Fruit.

455
00:17:41,246 --> 00:17:42,397
(Dropping food as it eats)

456
00:17:42,398 --> 00:17:43,398
Fascinating.

457
00:17:43,873 --> 00:17:44,966
Hello.

458
00:17:45,286 --> 00:17:47,502
Hello. Nice to meet you.

459
00:17:48,836 --> 00:17:50,836
I'm from Korea.

460
00:17:53,141 --> 00:17:54,308
It's looking down.

461
00:17:57,767 --> 00:17:59,247
We're fascinated by each other.

462
00:17:59,467 --> 00:18:00,548
This is fascinating.

463
00:18:01,327 --> 00:18:02,550
Should we take a photo together?

464
00:18:04,154 --> 00:18:05,586
- It's close.
- Can you see it?

465
00:18:05,921 --> 00:18:07,594
- It's here.
- Is it here?

466
00:18:07,607 --> 00:18:09,457
I think it's there. Or is that not it?

467
00:18:09,791 --> 00:18:10,725
I think that's it.

468
00:18:10,726 --> 00:18:14,699
(The orangutan in the middle)

469
00:18:16,419 --> 00:18:18,733
Hello.

470
00:18:20,835 --> 00:18:23,471
- This is amazing.
- We even watched them eat.

471
00:18:23,938 --> 00:18:26,674
The difference in size is enormous.

472
00:18:26,797 --> 00:18:29,850
- Exactly.
- The mom is huge, but the baby is tiny.

473
00:18:29,851 --> 00:18:30,978
This is fascinating.

474
00:18:33,530 --> 00:18:36,184
It's amazing how he walks barefoot.

475
00:18:38,595 --> 00:18:42,461
(Carefully following Ipu)

476
00:18:42,901 --> 00:18:45,193
There are monkeys.

477
00:18:45,221 --> 00:18:46,574
- Monkeys?
- Yes.

478
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:48,029
Another monkey?

479
00:18:48,419 --> 00:18:50,364
It's over there!

480
00:18:50,898 --> 00:18:51,899
That's a baby.

481
00:18:52,052 --> 00:18:53,167
A monkey is here?

482
00:18:53,168 --> 00:18:53,999
(Peeking out)

483
00:18:54,466 --> 00:18:55,736
There's a monkey?

484
00:18:56,137 --> 00:18:58,206
- So cute.
- It's close.

485
00:18:58,252 --> 00:18:59,640
It's passing in front of us.

486
00:18:59,641 --> 00:19:00,899
(A pig-tailed macaque)

487
00:19:01,709 --> 00:19:04,112
It's not the same kind as earlier.

488
00:19:04,812 --> 00:19:06,013
It's just a baby.

489
00:19:06,486 --> 00:19:07,849
So freaking cute.

490
00:19:07,999 --> 00:19:09,784
We're seeing many moms and babies today.

491
00:19:09,993 --> 00:19:11,586
And what's so cute is...

492
00:19:11,673 --> 00:19:14,589
- it touches the tree before going.
- Before crossing?

493
00:19:14,713 --> 00:19:17,591
- Like testing a bridge?
- Look before you leap.

494
00:19:17,671 --> 00:19:19,861
Shake a tree before climbing it.

495
00:19:20,684 --> 00:19:22,463
So cute.

496
00:19:22,464 --> 00:19:23,564
- My goodness.
- So cute.

497
00:19:23,565 --> 00:19:25,124
(An adorable baby monkey)

498
00:19:25,633 --> 00:19:27,368
It eats things off the tree.

499
00:19:27,704 --> 00:19:29,704
I can't handle how cute it is.

500
00:19:29,724 --> 00:19:30,872
I can't handle this.

501
00:19:30,918 --> 00:19:32,206
It's so cute.

502
00:19:32,863 --> 00:19:34,175
It looks just like a person.

503
00:19:34,223 --> 00:19:35,943
Its ears and ribs too.

504
00:19:37,178 --> 00:19:40,047
Our guide Ipu...

505
00:19:40,131 --> 00:19:40,830
(Monkey call)

506
00:19:40,831 --> 00:19:43,084
is great at spotting monkeys.

507
00:19:43,085 --> 00:19:43,918
(Monkey call)

508
00:19:45,498 --> 00:19:46,621
(Monkey call)

509
00:19:47,088 --> 00:19:48,055
(Imitating the call)

510
00:19:48,451 --> 00:19:49,457
(Monkey call)

511
00:19:49,518 --> 00:19:50,471
(Imitating the call)

512
00:19:50,485 --> 00:19:51,392
(Monkey call)

513
00:19:51,538 --> 00:19:52,460
(Imitating the call)

514
00:19:53,405 --> 00:19:56,631
But Ipu is amazing.
How does he know this path?

515
00:19:56,705 --> 00:19:58,032
- Right.
- He knows it by heart?

516
00:19:58,766 --> 00:20:00,968
He memorized every path.
That's so impressive.

517
00:20:01,029 --> 00:20:02,703
He must come here all the time, right?

518
00:20:06,263 --> 00:20:09,967
(Did Ipu find something else?)

519
00:20:10,803 --> 00:20:11,412
What is it?

520
00:20:11,514 --> 00:20:13,981
Why are you standing so solemnly, Ipu?

521
00:20:15,101 --> 00:20:16,350
You startled me.

522
00:20:16,473 --> 00:20:17,318
What is it?

523
00:20:17,341 --> 00:20:18,486
There must be something.

524
00:20:19,253 --> 00:20:20,354
What is it?

525
00:20:20,967 --> 00:20:22,156
What is it this time?

526
00:20:25,833 --> 00:20:26,961
That scared me.

527
00:20:26,962 --> 00:20:29,733
(Could something be wrong?)

528
00:20:30,313 --> 00:20:32,533
(Watching him carefully)

529
00:20:33,180 --> 00:20:34,335
You can eat fruit here.

530
00:20:36,300 --> 00:20:37,738
It must be time to eat fruit.

531
00:20:37,739 --> 00:20:39,020
(That's it?)

532
00:20:39,347 --> 00:20:42,680
But he sounded so serious saying it.

533
00:20:42,681 --> 00:20:43,778
That was scary.

534
00:20:43,779 --> 00:20:45,146
I thought there was a tiger.

535
00:20:45,826 --> 00:20:49,380
(The impersonation begins.)

536
00:20:49,767 --> 00:20:51,852
Eat fruit.

537
00:20:53,094 --> 00:20:54,827
It's very hot.

538
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:56,624
- "It's very hot, so come over here?"
- It's very hot?

539
00:20:56,678 --> 00:20:58,993
This is so funny.

540
00:20:59,393 --> 00:21:00,861
I'm losing it.

541
00:21:01,462 --> 00:21:02,363
"Very hot."

542
00:21:02,818 --> 00:21:04,365
Ipu is my type of guy.

543
00:21:05,132 --> 00:21:08,069
Which one of Ipu's rooms is this?

544
00:21:08,369 --> 00:21:10,538
- The 20th.
- The 20th?

545
00:21:10,657 --> 00:21:12,807
- He keeps searching for things.
- Exactly.

546
00:21:13,577 --> 00:21:15,009
How can he even see that?

547
00:21:15,884 --> 00:21:18,246
Just seeing this is incredible.

548
00:21:18,735 --> 00:21:19,880
And he keeps making this face.

549
00:21:21,249 --> 00:21:22,416
You're good at that.

550
00:21:22,417 --> 00:21:23,989
(Serious)

551
00:21:24,082 --> 00:21:25,186
That's good.

552
00:21:26,602 --> 00:21:28,435
Eat fruit.

553
00:21:28,921 --> 00:21:32,357
(Ipu has a character.)

554
00:21:33,493 --> 00:21:37,028
- This is so funny.
- He's different when looking at us...

555
00:21:37,029 --> 00:21:38,864
compared to when he's looking
for an orangutan.

556
00:21:38,865 --> 00:21:40,265
He goes like this.

557
00:21:40,266 --> 00:21:41,166
He's good at his job.

558
00:21:41,634 --> 00:21:43,234
I have some fruit for you.

559
00:21:43,603 --> 00:21:45,070
(Finally, it's break time!)

560
00:21:45,071 --> 00:21:46,238
What kind of fruit?

561
00:21:46,239 --> 00:21:48,206
I have some bananas, oranges,

562
00:21:48,541 --> 00:21:49,975
passion fruit,

563
00:21:49,976 --> 00:21:52,077
pineapple,

564
00:21:52,078 --> 00:21:53,178
and dragon fruit.

565
00:21:53,179 --> 00:21:55,080
Dragon fruit!

566
00:21:55,314 --> 00:21:56,848
That's quite a variety.

567
00:21:57,116 --> 00:21:59,851
He's even setting up seats for us
with the banana leaf.

568
00:21:59,852 --> 00:22:00,685
The banana leaf...

569
00:22:03,122 --> 00:22:05,924
(Eco-friendly sitting mat)

570
00:22:06,159 --> 00:22:08,060
I don't think that's our seat.

571
00:22:08,061 --> 00:22:09,261
It's probably going to be our dish.

572
00:22:09,262 --> 00:22:10,462
Oh, a dish.

573
00:22:10,463 --> 00:22:11,864
A fruit dish.

574
00:22:12,098 --> 00:22:13,598
That's how it was when I looked it up.

575
00:22:13,599 --> 00:22:15,567
- See? Research is important.
- I've seen it.

576
00:22:15,568 --> 00:22:17,035
- It's usually for the plate.
- I see.

577
00:22:17,036 --> 00:22:18,804
We almost sat on it.

578
00:22:18,805 --> 00:22:20,005
(Fruit dish almost became butt dish.)

579
00:22:21,807 --> 00:22:23,741
(Rustle)

580
00:22:23,843 --> 00:22:24,776
I see a monkey!

581
00:22:24,978 --> 00:22:27,278
Maybe he smelled the fruit.

582
00:22:27,279 --> 00:22:28,379
There he is.

583
00:22:28,614 --> 00:22:30,281
- Where do you see them?
- Over there.

584
00:22:30,282 --> 00:22:31,316
I see him.

585
00:22:31,751 --> 00:22:33,351
He has gray fur.

586
00:22:33,352 --> 00:22:36,455
I see another species.

587
00:22:37,056 --> 00:22:38,323
He looks like he's wearing a mask.

588
00:22:38,324 --> 00:22:40,392
He's leaning his head on the tree.

589
00:22:40,927 --> 00:22:42,594
He's so cute.
He looks like a penguin.

590
00:22:42,595 --> 00:22:43,629
(Spotted a surprisingly stylish monkey)

591
00:22:43,930 --> 00:22:46,731
He kind of looks like he's wearing
a Muay Thai mask.

592
00:22:46,933 --> 00:22:48,300
He reminds me of "King of Masked Singer."

593
00:22:48,434 --> 00:22:51,302
(Chuckle)

594
00:22:52,138 --> 00:22:53,639
He kind of does.

595
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:56,007
He can definitely enter
"King of Masked Singer."

596
00:22:56,008 --> 00:22:57,379
(Thomas's langur: endemic
to northern Sumatra,)

597
00:22:57,380 --> 00:22:58,777
(known for mask-like facial markings.)

598
00:22:58,944 --> 00:23:00,311
His tail is super long.

599
00:23:00,312 --> 00:23:02,514
Right.

600
00:23:02,515 --> 00:23:04,015
He has a long tail.

601
00:23:04,016 --> 00:23:06,351
His tail is longer than his body.

602
00:23:06,919 --> 00:23:08,153
He looks so mysterious.

603
00:23:08,154 --> 00:23:09,721
He's beautiful.

604
00:23:09,722 --> 00:23:12,090
How do you say "long tail" in Korean?

605
00:23:12,091 --> 00:23:14,359
"Gin kkori."

606
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:16,307
"Gin kkori wonsungi."

607
00:23:16,495 --> 00:23:17,695
"Gin kkori wonsungi."

608
00:23:18,598 --> 00:23:20,899
Your pronunciation is very good.

609
00:23:22,068 --> 00:23:23,402
Ipu's pronunciation is so good.

610
00:23:23,836 --> 00:23:28,173
(He can traverse the jungle
with a tail longer than his body.)

611
00:23:28,241 --> 00:23:29,174
Come this way.

612
00:23:29,576 --> 00:23:31,043
Ipu's telling us to come.

613
00:23:31,377 --> 00:23:34,646
- Let's go.
- He's so cute.

614
00:23:35,147 --> 00:23:36,214
Oh my god!

615
00:23:36,382 --> 00:23:38,049
He's right in front of us.
How cute.

616
00:23:39,852 --> 00:23:41,854
- He seems shy.
- His tail is super long.

617
00:23:41,855 --> 00:23:43,521
The way he's perched is so cute.

618
00:23:43,522 --> 00:23:46,291
(Saying hello up close.)

619
00:23:46,626 --> 00:23:47,926
His head is so small.

620
00:23:48,194 --> 00:23:50,128
Doesn't he remind you of Sun Wukong?

621
00:23:50,129 --> 00:23:51,430
He looks like a character
from "Romance of the Three Kingdoms."

622
00:23:51,431 --> 00:23:52,897
I think it's his hair.

623
00:23:52,898 --> 00:23:55,000
He has an edgy hairstyle.

624
00:23:55,301 --> 00:23:56,434
He kind of does.

625
00:23:56,435 --> 00:23:57,302
I like it.

626
00:23:57,303 --> 00:23:59,604
His hairstyle is cool.

627
00:23:59,605 --> 00:24:01,873
- He must groom himself well.
- He has a mohawk hairstyle.

628
00:24:01,874 --> 00:24:03,608
He's very cool. So funky.

629
00:24:04,143 --> 00:24:05,009
Let's go back.

630
00:24:05,244 --> 00:24:08,546
I think our fruit is almost ready.

631
00:24:08,981 --> 00:24:09,847
Let's go.

632
00:24:10,416 --> 00:24:11,683
That was so cute.

633
00:24:11,684 --> 00:24:12,617
Right, he was so cute.

634
00:24:13,019 --> 00:24:14,586
Oh, we meet again.

635
00:24:15,254 --> 00:24:16,421
Won Ji, he's here again.

636
00:24:16,856 --> 00:24:18,190
- He's Won Ji's favorite.
- Just a second.

637
00:24:18,625 --> 00:24:20,224
I'm going to interview him.

638
00:24:20,559 --> 00:24:21,425
How are you?

639
00:24:21,861 --> 00:24:22,861
What's your name?

640
00:24:22,862 --> 00:24:24,362
(Puzzled)

641
00:24:24,363 --> 00:24:25,330
John.

642
00:24:25,331 --> 00:24:27,165
- Are you from Indonesia?
- Yes.

643
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:29,234
Are you part of our team?

644
00:24:29,535 --> 00:24:34,372
Yeah, I'm the park security here.

645
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:37,275
We met three times, remember?

646
00:24:37,276 --> 00:24:38,276
Yeah.

647
00:24:39,145 --> 00:24:41,747
- So that's why he was everywhere.
- He was the security.

648
00:24:42,281 --> 00:24:44,048
- You're the security.
- The security.

649
00:24:44,850 --> 00:24:46,818
Thank you so much.

650
00:24:46,819 --> 00:24:47,952
Thank you.

651
00:24:48,154 --> 00:24:50,021
Finally, the mystery solves itself.

652
00:24:50,022 --> 00:24:51,890
I thought he was part of our team.

653
00:24:53,125 --> 00:24:56,094
(The fruits are still being prepared.)

654
00:24:56,095 --> 00:24:58,731
(Rustle)

655
00:24:58,732 --> 00:25:00,231
Look, look!

656
00:25:00,232 --> 00:25:02,233
- The monkey came.
- They must be here for the fruit.

657
00:25:02,501 --> 00:25:04,569
- Do you think it's the same one?
- Let's invite them over.

658
00:25:04,570 --> 00:25:05,570
Oh, it's peeing.

659
00:25:06,639 --> 00:25:08,440
It would be so funny if it peed here.

660
00:25:08,908 --> 00:25:10,108
Is it the same monkey from before?

661
00:25:10,743 --> 00:25:12,911
It must have smelled the fruit.

662
00:25:12,912 --> 00:25:14,846
It's practically drooling already.

663
00:25:15,081 --> 00:25:16,214
Hey, don't poop here, okay?

664
00:25:17,383 --> 00:25:18,750
There are some monkeys above us too.

665
00:25:18,751 --> 00:25:20,218
There are so many.

666
00:25:20,486 --> 00:25:22,520
They must have smelled our fruit.

667
00:25:22,922 --> 00:25:24,155
It's super crowded up there.

668
00:25:24,290 --> 00:25:25,957
They must be waiting until we leave.

669
00:25:26,092 --> 00:25:28,560
They're waiting for our leftovers.

670
00:25:28,928 --> 00:25:30,061
"Slurp."

671
00:25:32,498 --> 00:25:33,631
Look over there!

672
00:25:33,933 --> 00:25:34,799
Where?

673
00:25:36,035 --> 00:25:37,202
We're surrounded.

674
00:25:37,837 --> 00:25:39,304
There's one there...

675
00:25:39,305 --> 00:25:40,238
and another over there.

676
00:25:40,673 --> 00:25:43,441
- Look over there.
- We're surrounded.

677
00:25:43,608 --> 00:25:45,109
I think I see a baby monkey.

678
00:25:46,846 --> 00:25:48,213
There's a baby over there.

679
00:25:48,714 --> 00:25:50,815
How young do you think it is?
Looks very young.

680
00:25:51,584 --> 00:25:53,418
It's right next to her.

681
00:25:54,320 --> 00:25:55,320
Look at the baby.

682
00:25:55,321 --> 00:25:56,421
(Fluffy baby monkey)

683
00:25:56,422 --> 00:25:58,823
- So small.
- They're so cute.

684
00:25:58,824 --> 00:25:59,757
Super cute.

685
00:26:00,793 --> 00:26:02,393
How adorable.

686
00:26:03,028 --> 00:26:04,028
Such a baby, right?

687
00:26:04,930 --> 00:26:06,731
Could it be a newborn?

688
00:26:07,700 --> 00:26:08,767
I see one over there, too.

689
00:26:08,768 --> 00:26:09,635
(Amazed)

690
00:26:09,636 --> 00:26:10,602
So cute.

691
00:26:10,770 --> 00:26:12,070
The baby monkey...

692
00:26:12,071 --> 00:26:13,772
is so cute.

693
00:26:13,773 --> 00:26:14,605
(Amazed and excited)

694
00:26:14,606 --> 00:26:15,507
There's one over there, too.

695
00:26:16,575 --> 00:26:18,309
This is so amazing.

696
00:26:18,310 --> 00:26:21,546
(Slipping back to mom's arms)

697
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:23,114
Now, let's eat the fruit.

698
00:26:23,416 --> 00:26:24,315
Wow.

699
00:26:25,284 --> 00:26:26,384
This is so pretty.

700
00:26:27,319 --> 00:26:29,453
The watermelon's so red.

701
00:26:29,822 --> 00:26:31,456
The colors are beautiful.

702
00:26:31,457 --> 00:26:32,423
Look at the watermelon.

703
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:33,591
I see mandarin oranges, too.

704
00:26:33,592 --> 00:26:34,793
(Colors blended by nature)

705
00:26:34,794 --> 00:26:36,528
It's so pretty.

706
00:26:36,529 --> 00:26:39,497
Look, he sandwiched passionfruit
between pineapple slices.

707
00:26:39,966 --> 00:26:41,032
True foodie.

708
00:26:41,033 --> 00:26:42,780
(He knows what he's doing
as a legendary foodie.)

709
00:26:42,780 --> 00:26:44,573
"True foodie."

710
00:26:44,770 --> 00:26:46,304
A culinary genius.

711
00:26:46,305 --> 00:26:48,506
This is so refreshing.

712
00:26:48,974 --> 00:26:50,541
We have oranges and bananas.

713
00:26:50,542 --> 00:26:52,710
How pretty.

714
00:26:52,846 --> 00:26:54,346
They took such care.

715
00:26:54,347 --> 00:26:55,380
(Decorated with flowers.)

716
00:26:55,381 --> 00:26:56,882
The colors are arranged so beautifully.

717
00:26:57,483 --> 00:26:58,883
So pretty.

718
00:26:58,884 --> 00:27:00,585
(Almost too pretty to eat)

719
00:27:00,586 --> 00:27:02,420
You can eat now.

720
00:27:02,421 --> 00:27:04,856
- Thank you!
- Thank you for the fruit.

721
00:27:05,124 --> 00:27:07,959
Watermelons are my favorite.

722
00:27:08,494 --> 00:27:10,528
(Chomp)

723
00:27:11,363 --> 00:27:12,363
This is so sweet.

724
00:27:13,065 --> 00:27:14,198
Getting my daily dose of vitamins!

725
00:27:15,401 --> 00:27:16,301
It's incredibly sweet.

726
00:27:16,735 --> 00:27:19,003
The pineapple-passionfruit sandwich
is so good.

727
00:27:19,338 --> 00:27:20,938
Pineapples are so tangy.

728
00:27:20,939 --> 00:27:21,806
It's good, right?

729
00:27:21,807 --> 00:27:24,008
- It's very refreshing.
- He's indeed a foodie expert.

730
00:27:25,110 --> 00:27:28,145
(Getting proper vitamins)

731
00:27:28,614 --> 00:27:32,183
(Some fruit for Ipu
after all his hard work.)

732
00:27:32,184 --> 00:27:32,917
Ipu,

733
00:27:33,219 --> 00:27:34,853
can I have one mandarin orange?

734
00:27:36,255 --> 00:27:37,388
Just one.

735
00:27:38,958 --> 00:27:40,458
He gave me two.

736
00:27:40,759 --> 00:27:41,659
Do you want some?

737
00:27:41,660 --> 00:27:44,528
(Resorts to stealing fruit
because it's so good.)

738
00:27:45,998 --> 00:27:47,131
The mandarin orange is so delicious.

739
00:27:48,467 --> 00:27:50,067
I feel recharged.

740
00:27:51,837 --> 00:27:53,237
Do you want to try this one, too?

741
00:27:53,238 --> 00:27:54,939
I want to try.

742
00:27:55,374 --> 00:27:56,374
Thank you.

743
00:27:56,375 --> 00:27:57,241
What is it?

744
00:27:57,576 --> 00:27:59,210
That's snake fruit.

745
00:27:59,478 --> 00:28:01,683
(Salak: a tropical fruit
often called snakefruit...)

746
00:28:01,684 --> 00:28:03,214
(due to its scaly skin.)

747
00:28:03,382 --> 00:28:05,450
How do we eat this? Do we just peel it?

748
00:28:05,451 --> 00:28:07,118
Oh, you just peel it.

749
00:28:07,119 --> 00:28:08,820
(White flesh exposed when peeled off)

750
00:28:08,821 --> 00:28:10,555
Like garlic?

751
00:28:10,723 --> 00:28:12,457
(Chomp after making it bite-sized)

752
00:28:12,458 --> 00:28:13,291
Okay.

753
00:28:14,126 --> 00:28:16,127
- Do we put the peels here?
- Yeah.

754
00:28:16,128 --> 00:28:16,928
Okay.

755
00:28:17,463 --> 00:28:18,396
It's delicious.

756
00:28:19,098 --> 00:28:19,964
Do you want to try?

757
00:28:20,099 --> 00:28:20,999
It smells nice.

758
00:28:21,500 --> 00:28:22,433
It's tangy.

759
00:28:22,434 --> 00:28:23,868
(Nom)

760
00:28:27,106 --> 00:28:29,140
It tastes like chestnuts but sour.

761
00:28:29,675 --> 00:28:31,876
Do you not like it? I like its aroma.

762
00:28:32,712 --> 00:28:33,845
You have to take out the seed.

763
00:28:35,481 --> 00:28:37,416
(Chomp)

764
00:28:37,417 --> 00:28:39,084
The fruit inside is delicious.

765
00:28:39,818 --> 00:28:41,752
Can this cause diarrhea?

766
00:28:41,753 --> 00:28:42,820
No, no.

767
00:28:42,821 --> 00:28:43,854
It prevents diarrhea.

768
00:28:43,855 --> 00:28:45,256
So it's the opposite.

769
00:28:45,924 --> 00:28:47,659
When you have a stomachache,

770
00:28:47,660 --> 00:28:48,760
eating this would stop it?

771
00:28:48,761 --> 00:28:50,628
So it works like anti-diarrhea medicine.

772
00:28:50,629 --> 00:28:51,729
Right.

773
00:28:51,830 --> 00:28:52,863
I think it's a good idea to eat this.

774
00:28:52,864 --> 00:28:55,099
We would be in trouble if we need
to go number 2 in the jungle.

775
00:28:59,104 --> 00:29:00,638
Do you want to see a magic trick?

776
00:29:01,206 --> 00:29:03,541
(Bring it already.)

777
00:29:03,542 --> 00:29:04,875
He's going to show us a magic trick.

778
00:29:12,518 --> 00:29:13,952
Is there anything he can't do?

779
00:29:16,221 --> 00:29:17,988
What if all the monkeys gather around?

780
00:29:18,824 --> 00:29:19,857
Wow.

781
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:22,393
It's magic plastic.

782
00:29:22,394 --> 00:29:23,895
He's really good.

783
00:29:23,896 --> 00:29:25,430
Ipu the piper.

784
00:29:25,431 --> 00:29:26,264
Wow.

785
00:29:26,265 --> 00:29:27,365
(Ipu can do anything.)

786
00:29:27,800 --> 00:29:29,501
Do you want to see another trick?

787
00:29:29,502 --> 00:29:31,102
Second magic trick?

788
00:29:31,637 --> 00:29:33,805
(Open)

789
00:29:36,342 --> 00:29:37,208
Where did he come from?

790
00:29:37,242 --> 00:29:38,042
(It's a snake!)

791
00:29:38,377 --> 00:29:40,511
It's a real snake.

792
00:29:40,614 --> 00:29:42,981
(Shocked)

793
00:29:43,215 --> 00:29:44,115
Wow.

794
00:29:44,116 --> 00:29:47,385
(Snake engaging with his core)

795
00:29:47,786 --> 00:29:49,320
(Flicking his tongue.)

796
00:29:49,688 --> 00:29:51,889
Is it okay to do that?

797
00:29:52,558 --> 00:29:53,591
(Folding him neatly)

798
00:29:55,594 --> 00:29:56,494
(Ah)

799
00:29:56,495 --> 00:29:58,463
No, don't do that.

800
00:29:58,797 --> 00:29:59,997
Is it even safe?

801
00:30:01,066 --> 00:30:03,067
(He put the snake in his mouth.)

802
00:30:03,068 --> 00:30:04,135
Is he really doing this?

803
00:30:04,136 --> 00:30:05,722
(Do not attempt.)

804
00:30:05,723 --> 00:30:08,239
(This was filmed safely
with a trained professional.)

805
00:30:08,307 --> 00:30:11,310
(Shocked)

806
00:30:11,311 --> 00:30:12,277
That's crazy.

807
00:30:12,278 --> 00:30:14,245
Wow, I can't believe it.

808
00:30:14,546 --> 00:30:15,679
Amazing.

809
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:16,747
(A jaw-dropping stunt)

810
00:30:17,716 --> 00:30:22,119
(Snake coming out of the mouth)

811
00:30:22,988 --> 00:30:24,121
Wow.

812
00:30:24,556 --> 00:30:25,789
Did he eat the snake?

813
00:30:25,891 --> 00:30:26,958
Wait.

814
00:30:28,293 --> 00:30:29,893
It's like kissing.

815
00:30:29,894 --> 00:30:31,395
Oh my gosh.

816
00:30:31,396 --> 00:30:33,931
I guess that snake isn't venomous.

817
00:30:34,034 --> 00:30:36,167
He could give Mr. Kim Byung-man
a run for his money.

818
00:30:36,168 --> 00:30:36,901
Right.

819
00:30:36,902 --> 00:30:38,570
The snake looks so harmless.

820
00:30:38,571 --> 00:30:39,571
It's kind of cute.

821
00:30:39,572 --> 00:30:40,872
What a derpy little noodle.

822
00:30:40,873 --> 00:30:44,209
The way it's hissing reminds me
of a chihuahua barking.

823
00:30:44,943 --> 00:30:45,743
He's so small.

824
00:30:45,744 --> 00:30:46,577
Come on.

825
00:30:47,179 --> 00:30:48,112
Can I touch it?

826
00:30:49,281 --> 00:30:50,648
(Slip)

827
00:30:50,649 --> 00:30:51,883
I want to touch it too.

828
00:30:51,884 --> 00:30:54,085
Don't tease me, okay?

829
00:30:54,820 --> 00:30:57,155
- "Don't tease me."
- Good snake.

830
00:30:57,156 --> 00:30:57,989
(Tremble)

831
00:30:57,990 --> 00:31:00,595
She's always so scared,
but she still wants to touch.

832
00:31:01,627 --> 00:31:02,494
(She's a brave scaredy cat.)

833
00:31:02,501 --> 00:31:04,101
Curiosity got the best of me.

834
00:31:05,798 --> 00:31:07,599
(Trying again)

835
00:31:08,133 --> 00:31:10,201
She got up the courage.

836
00:31:10,202 --> 00:31:11,368
(Frowning)

837
00:31:11,369 --> 00:31:12,303
(Jump)

838
00:31:12,838 --> 00:31:15,073
(Teasing the scaredy cat for fun)

839
00:31:15,074 --> 00:31:15,940
So cute.

840
00:31:15,941 --> 00:31:18,576
- It's slippery. Touch it.
- Oh gosh!

841
00:31:18,911 --> 00:31:20,111
Slippery.

842
00:31:20,112 --> 00:31:21,513
(Too fun not to do it again.)

843
00:31:21,514 --> 00:31:22,881
Okay, let's get back to the jungle.

844
00:31:22,882 --> 00:31:24,983
Okay, back to the jungle.

845
00:31:24,984 --> 00:31:27,085
- Are you leaving?
- Goodbye!

846
00:31:27,086 --> 00:31:28,319
(Thanks for bearing with us.)

847
00:31:28,517 --> 00:31:29,786
This is so much fun.

848
00:31:30,020 --> 00:31:31,388
So fun.

849
00:31:32,289 --> 00:31:33,711
They keep coming down.

850
00:31:33,712 --> 00:31:35,425
There's one more.

851
00:31:36,299 --> 00:31:40,099
- I think they want to eat the fruit.
- Yeah.

852
00:31:40,165 --> 00:31:42,085
Are we allowed to feed them?

853
00:31:42,086 --> 00:31:43,033
- No.
- Okay.

854
00:31:43,146 --> 00:31:44,668
It's just for people?

855
00:31:44,779 --> 00:31:45,802
Yes, for people only.

856
00:31:45,803 --> 00:31:47,469
Not for animals.

857
00:31:47,476 --> 00:31:49,117
(Feeding wildlife is strictly prohibited
to protect the ecosystem.)

858
00:31:49,297 --> 00:31:52,737
After we're done,
let's go to our campsite.

859
00:31:52,750 --> 00:31:54,310
It takes another two hours.

860
00:31:54,311 --> 00:31:56,443
- Two hours?
- You can finish the fruit first.

861
00:31:56,583 --> 00:31:57,814
Uphills and downhills.

862
00:31:57,903 --> 00:32:00,083
- After we finish eating?
- Yes.

863
00:32:00,263 --> 00:32:01,385
We've charged our energy!

864
00:32:02,052 --> 00:32:04,983
He says the uphills and downhills
come after this.

865
00:32:04,984 --> 00:32:06,609
- So eat up.
- Got it.

866
00:32:06,723 --> 00:32:08,825
Okay. Let's go to camp
after we finish this.

867
00:32:08,826 --> 00:32:09,660
Okay.

868
00:32:10,026 --> 00:32:11,395
Follow Ipu.

869
00:32:11,906 --> 00:32:13,263
We follow Ipu.

870
00:32:13,264 --> 00:32:17,601
Let's go together.

871
00:32:18,366 --> 00:32:19,919
(Indonesia)

872
00:32:20,539 --> 00:32:24,626
(They'll be traveling
for another two hours.)

873
00:32:25,479 --> 00:32:28,159
(Back on the trail with music)

874
00:32:28,252 --> 00:32:31,748
<i>- Abra-ca-Empty
- Abra-ca-Empty</i>

875
00:32:32,239 --> 00:32:34,999
(Can't have a jungle without this song!)

876
00:32:36,846 --> 00:32:38,846
<i>- Let it all go</i>
<i>- Let it all go</i>

877
00:32:38,885 --> 00:32:40,257
<i>- Get rid of it
- Get rid of it</i>

878
00:32:40,325 --> 00:32:42,359
<i>Get rid of it all!</i>

879
00:32:43,058 --> 00:32:45,058
We really got rid of it all today.

880
00:32:45,188 --> 00:32:46,163
- We really did.
- True.

881
00:32:46,164 --> 00:32:47,764
This song's a bop.

882
00:32:49,112 --> 00:32:52,402
This is where the real trek begins.

883
00:32:54,696 --> 00:32:57,040
The vines have turned into stairs.

884
00:32:57,741 --> 00:32:58,842
Vine stairs.

885
00:33:01,041 --> 00:33:05,182
Talk about hitting the vine jackpot.

886
00:33:07,527 --> 00:33:12,155
Forget deep roots.
We've got the whole vine now.

887
00:33:13,841 --> 00:33:15,258
We've come down a long way.

888
00:33:15,394 --> 00:33:16,326
Right?

889
00:33:16,893 --> 00:33:19,468
You can see some houses down there.

890
00:33:19,469 --> 00:33:20,430
It's a village.

891
00:33:20,458 --> 00:33:21,698
Ipu.

892
00:33:21,737 --> 00:33:23,033
Is that our camp?

893
00:33:23,571 --> 00:33:25,083
Not now.

894
00:33:25,084 --> 00:33:26,398
Two more hours to go.

895
00:33:26,484 --> 00:33:27,571
- Two hours?
- Two hours?

896
00:33:27,638 --> 00:33:29,072
- Another two hours?
- He says it's not here.

897
00:33:29,955 --> 00:33:32,095
Two hours of uphill and downhill.

898
00:33:32,096 --> 00:33:33,610
So it starts now.

899
00:33:33,682 --> 00:33:35,045
I guess we have to go up once.

900
00:33:35,855 --> 00:33:39,722
- Up and down.
- He says it keeps coming.

901
00:33:39,782 --> 00:33:41,618
<i>Up, down, up, up, down</i>

902
00:33:42,060 --> 00:33:44,727
(Singing their worries away)

903
00:33:44,960 --> 00:33:46,023
She's so funny.

904
00:33:46,590 --> 00:33:47,791
My kind of humor.

905
00:33:49,579 --> 00:33:52,029
I can hear something refreshing.

906
00:33:52,631 --> 00:33:53,430
Huh?

907
00:33:53,891 --> 00:33:54,865
What?

908
00:33:56,333 --> 00:33:57,618
We're crossing over water?

909
00:33:57,619 --> 00:34:01,004
I don't see any way around the water.

910
00:34:01,225 --> 00:34:02,739
Ipu!

911
00:34:03,085 --> 00:34:04,951
- Do we have to go there?
- Yeah.

912
00:34:05,509 --> 00:34:07,310
Seriously?

913
00:34:07,311 --> 00:34:09,469
(A wild stream appears.)

914
00:34:09,962 --> 00:34:12,416
So this is why Ipu came barefoot.

915
00:34:12,949 --> 00:34:14,618
Do we have to take our shoes off?

916
00:34:15,385 --> 00:34:16,853
I think we're just going to get wet.

917
00:34:17,049 --> 00:34:18,321
We keep them on.

918
00:34:18,922 --> 00:34:20,922
I guess it's better than going barefoot.

919
00:34:21,596 --> 00:34:22,789
Be careful.

920
00:34:22,942 --> 00:34:24,394
Be careful.

921
00:34:25,729 --> 00:34:27,864
Wow, it's really steep.

922
00:34:27,982 --> 00:34:29,566
Careful, it's slippery.

923
00:34:30,033 --> 00:34:32,069
- Be careful, everyone!
- Okay.

924
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:33,696
(Carefully)

925
00:34:34,002 --> 00:34:35,105
(Slippery)

926
00:34:35,106 --> 00:34:36,039
Watch your steps.

927
00:34:36,109 --> 00:34:38,675
Please keep a safe distance.

928
00:34:38,676 --> 00:34:40,922
(Wet ground means
keeping your distance is a must.)

929
00:34:44,289 --> 00:34:47,884
It's like a refreshing little waterfall.

930
00:34:48,452 --> 00:34:49,853
It looks so refreshing!

931
00:34:50,353 --> 00:34:53,040
Wow, it really feels refreshing.

932
00:34:53,060 --> 00:34:54,480
- It's so different.
- I want to dip my feet in so bad.

933
00:34:55,358 --> 00:34:57,594
I'm going to wash my hands and my face.

934
00:34:57,665 --> 00:34:59,996
Wow, so cold!

935
00:35:03,018 --> 00:35:03,932
This feels so good.

936
00:35:04,178 --> 00:35:09,039
(Feels like the heat just melted away)

937
00:35:09,092 --> 00:35:10,373
Should I try dipping my feet in?

938
00:35:10,612 --> 00:35:11,608
Let's do it.

939
00:35:12,092 --> 00:35:13,510
Shall we?

940
00:35:14,329 --> 00:35:15,344
(Rolling up the pants)

941
00:35:15,345 --> 00:35:17,746
I think it'd be less slippery
with shoes on.

942
00:35:19,792 --> 00:35:21,751
Wow, it's so cold.

943
00:35:22,422 --> 00:35:24,521
- Did you just walk in?
- Yeah!

944
00:35:26,123 --> 00:35:27,624
It's so refreshing. I want to stay here.

945
00:35:27,922 --> 00:35:28,962
- Seriously.
- Really?

946
00:35:28,963 --> 00:35:30,648
I want to lie down here.

947
00:35:30,649 --> 00:35:31,561
Me too.

948
00:35:31,995 --> 00:35:34,531
Just letting go
and getting my shoes soaked...

949
00:35:35,132 --> 00:35:36,800
feels so damn good.

950
00:35:37,734 --> 00:35:38,835
I want to jump in.

951
00:35:38,836 --> 00:35:41,738
The water in my shoes...

952
00:35:42,973 --> 00:35:44,675
feels so weird.

953
00:35:44,676 --> 00:35:46,376
But I don't want to leave.

954
00:35:46,423 --> 00:35:48,979
Because leaving this place
is probably going to feel worse.

955
00:35:48,996 --> 00:35:50,996
I'm feeling exactly that right now.

956
00:35:51,123 --> 00:35:52,516
It feels pretty bad.

957
00:35:53,016 --> 00:35:54,902
But we're probably going to get
wet again, right?

958
00:35:54,903 --> 00:35:56,853
- Of course.
- Up and down.

959
00:35:56,983 --> 00:35:59,289
Just when our shoes start to dry,
it's downhill again.

960
00:35:59,430 --> 00:36:00,357
Alright.

961
00:36:00,416 --> 00:36:01,358
Let's go.

962
00:36:01,359 --> 00:36:03,819
Okay, let's go!

963
00:36:03,820 --> 00:36:05,987
(After a brief break, they keep going.)

964
00:36:06,716 --> 00:36:09,466
Shoes are a little slippery
now that they're wet.

965
00:36:09,467 --> 00:36:11,368
Be careful.

966
00:36:11,541 --> 00:36:13,270
It's pretty steep.

967
00:36:13,934 --> 00:36:15,138
Ugh.

968
00:36:15,588 --> 00:36:16,940
Darn.

969
00:36:17,240 --> 00:36:19,643
Gosh.

970
00:36:20,277 --> 00:36:22,546
Wait, is it all uphill from here?

971
00:36:23,605 --> 00:36:25,692
Up down.

972
00:36:25,939 --> 00:36:27,939
- Everyone okay?
- I'm okay.

973
00:36:27,940 --> 00:36:29,953
- Yes.
- Thank you.

974
00:36:30,560 --> 00:36:32,793
(Already two hours into the jungle trek)

975
00:36:33,613 --> 00:36:36,206
(Even Miss Sunshine is out of smiles.)

976
00:36:37,360 --> 00:36:39,764
Just a moment.

977
00:36:40,444 --> 00:36:42,832
We must be at least halfway there, right?

978
00:36:43,717 --> 00:36:45,700
Two more hours of up and down.

979
00:36:45,701 --> 00:36:46,764
Two more hours?

980
00:36:46,765 --> 00:36:48,972
- Why isn't the time reduced?
- Can we just sleep here?

981
00:36:49,482 --> 00:36:50,774
How's there still that much time left?

982
00:36:51,608 --> 00:36:53,843
An hour ago,
you said it'll take two hours.

983
00:36:53,849 --> 00:36:55,617
And now, you're telling us
there are two more hours.

984
00:36:55,618 --> 00:36:56,580
To make you happy.

985
00:36:56,689 --> 00:36:57,569
(Pause)

986
00:36:57,702 --> 00:36:59,702
Why do you keep saying...

987
00:36:59,722 --> 00:37:01,722
there are two hours left?

988
00:37:01,742 --> 00:37:03,742
I want to make you feel happy.

989
00:37:03,756 --> 00:37:05,822
- I'm not happy.
- "Two hours left."

990
00:37:06,890 --> 00:37:08,992
It's not even 40 minutes or something.

991
00:37:09,021 --> 00:37:11,021
But 2 hours feels so far away.

992
00:37:11,094 --> 00:37:13,230
There's only so much false hope
we can take.

993
00:37:13,261 --> 00:37:15,261
This isn't false hope. It's just torture!

994
00:37:16,781 --> 00:37:19,405
Can you smell it?

995
00:37:19,669 --> 00:37:22,339
He's really good at distracting us.

996
00:37:22,359 --> 00:37:23,359
Do you see that mountain?

997
00:37:24,005 --> 00:37:26,225
Two more hours of up and down
until we reach there.

998
00:37:26,332 --> 00:37:29,419
- That mountain?
- Yeah.

999
00:37:29,725 --> 00:37:32,612
Two more hours of up and down.

1000
00:37:32,779 --> 00:37:34,912
I don't like that.

1001
00:37:34,925 --> 00:37:36,025
- Why?
- Why?

1002
00:37:36,205 --> 00:37:37,887
Who could do it?

1003
00:37:37,952 --> 00:37:39,589
- You.
- Me?

1004
00:37:40,318 --> 00:37:41,258
Let me see.

1005
00:37:41,286 --> 00:37:43,159
Can you sleep in the jungle?

1006
00:37:43,460 --> 00:37:45,295
"Let me see."

1007
00:37:45,479 --> 00:37:47,197
"Let me see," she says.

1008
00:37:47,779 --> 00:37:50,026
Let's go with orangutans.

1009
00:37:50,126 --> 00:37:52,869
Okay, with orangutans!

1010
00:37:53,197 --> 00:37:54,570
With orangutans!

1011
00:37:54,571 --> 00:37:55,930
With orangutans,

1012
00:37:55,931 --> 00:37:58,008
we can do everything!

1013
00:37:58,497 --> 00:38:04,381
- With orangutans!
- Yeah, let's go!

1014
00:38:04,528 --> 00:38:06,950
I love the energy.

1015
00:38:07,415 --> 00:38:08,385
This is crazy.

1016
00:38:08,386 --> 00:38:10,902
(After all that uphill...)

1017
00:38:11,875 --> 00:38:17,326
(Now it's endless downhill.)

1018
00:38:19,106 --> 00:38:23,033
(30 minutes into the downhill course)

1019
00:38:23,326 --> 00:38:25,326
- Are you okay?
- Yes!

1020
00:38:25,484 --> 00:38:27,537
- It's okay. I'm okay.
- Is number 1 okay?

1021
00:38:27,697 --> 00:38:29,806
Number 1 is not okay.

1022
00:38:30,373 --> 00:38:31,983
- Is number 2 okay?
- Number 3, no.

1023
00:38:31,984 --> 00:38:34,010
Number 2 is okay!

1024
00:38:34,377 --> 00:38:36,468
Alright, even numbers!

1025
00:38:36,469 --> 00:38:39,502
Odd and even!

1026
00:38:39,695 --> 00:38:42,185
Odd numbers are not okay,
even numbers are okay.

1027
00:38:42,835 --> 00:38:44,275
I can call for a helicopter later.

1028
00:38:44,309 --> 00:38:45,722
- Huh?
- A helicopter.

1029
00:38:45,755 --> 00:38:46,856
An elephant?

1030
00:38:46,857 --> 00:38:47,724
Helicopter!

1031
00:38:47,725 --> 00:38:48,958
- Helicopter.
- An elephant?

1032
00:38:49,017 --> 00:38:50,827
Helicopter!

1033
00:38:50,857 --> 00:38:52,128
Chuff!

1034
00:38:52,550 --> 00:38:53,863
She's gone mad.

1035
00:38:53,864 --> 00:38:55,732
The heat's gotten into her.

1036
00:38:55,733 --> 00:38:57,200
Good lord.

1037
00:38:59,040 --> 00:39:00,136
She's gone crazy!

1038
00:39:00,137 --> 00:39:01,626
(Random bursts of high energy)

1039
00:39:04,386 --> 00:39:05,342
Ipu.

1040
00:39:05,419 --> 00:39:06,759
- Are you tired?
- No.

1041
00:39:06,792 --> 00:39:08,452
- But you look tired.
- No.

1042
00:39:09,479 --> 00:39:10,780
- You look tired.
- I saw that.

1043
00:39:12,932 --> 00:39:14,265
(You definitely sighed just now.)

1044
00:39:14,704 --> 00:39:15,957
- Tired.
- You?

1045
00:39:16,058 --> 00:39:17,187
- You.
- Not me.

1046
00:39:17,188 --> 00:39:18,021
Not me, he says.

1047
00:39:18,144 --> 00:39:19,155
Okay.

1048
00:39:19,489 --> 00:39:21,157
Let me see.

1049
00:39:21,758 --> 00:39:22,892
Ipu.

1050
00:39:23,226 --> 00:39:24,661
Does the campsite...

1051
00:39:24,971 --> 00:39:26,296
have snakes there?

1052
00:39:26,824 --> 00:39:28,611
- Snakes at the campsite?
- Yes, snakes.

1053
00:39:28,938 --> 00:39:30,367
Only crocodiles.

1054
00:39:30,431 --> 00:39:31,968
Only crocodiles?

1055
00:39:31,969 --> 00:39:33,069
Crocodiles?

1056
00:39:33,151 --> 00:39:34,404
What about tigers?

1057
00:39:34,711 --> 00:39:35,872
Tigers are already gone.

1058
00:39:35,873 --> 00:39:37,374
Already gone? Where to?

1059
00:39:37,966 --> 00:39:38,908
Where did they go?

1060
00:39:39,866 --> 00:39:42,160
(Ipu picks something up
instead of answering.)

1061
00:39:42,186 --> 00:39:44,447
Ipu, what's that?

1062
00:39:44,692 --> 00:39:45,749
Fruit.

1063
00:39:45,793 --> 00:39:46,826
- Fruit?
- Yes.

1064
00:39:48,218 --> 00:39:49,652
That's what gets me. So funny.

1065
00:39:49,700 --> 00:39:52,055
He can't be bothered to answer.

1066
00:39:52,100 --> 00:39:52,922
He's tired.

1067
00:39:52,960 --> 00:39:54,991
- Are you tired?
- No.

1068
00:39:55,073 --> 00:39:56,126
No?

1069
00:39:56,493 --> 00:39:57,727
What fruit is it?

1070
00:39:58,306 --> 00:39:59,926
(Endless questions)

1071
00:40:01,606 --> 00:40:03,700
He danced instead of answering me.

1072
00:40:03,860 --> 00:40:06,301
- He seems tired.
- Very.

1073
00:40:07,103 --> 00:40:09,439
We have two hours left.

1074
00:40:10,006 --> 00:40:11,515
You've got this, right?

1075
00:40:11,516 --> 00:40:12,675
You've got this.

1076
00:40:12,836 --> 00:40:14,144
He's so funny.

1077
00:40:16,689 --> 00:40:18,209
There's water.

1078
00:40:18,542 --> 00:40:19,883
Wow, a creek!

1079
00:40:21,416 --> 00:40:23,253
Our shower place!

1080
00:40:23,254 --> 00:40:26,808
(A river appears beyond the dense jungle.)

1081
00:40:27,908 --> 00:40:31,188
(The current looks pretty strong.)

1082
00:40:31,554 --> 00:40:33,247
You can swim here.

1083
00:40:33,268 --> 00:40:34,264
- What did you say?
- What?

1084
00:40:34,341 --> 00:40:36,399
We're crossing the river?

1085
00:40:36,681 --> 00:40:38,535
- Yes.
- Wow, okay.

1086
00:40:39,402 --> 00:40:41,438
We just jump in there?

1087
00:40:41,515 --> 00:40:44,240
The current's pretty strong here.

1088
00:40:44,415 --> 00:40:45,241
Liar!

1089
00:40:45,429 --> 00:40:46,807
You're a liar.

1090
00:40:46,808 --> 00:40:48,111
(They have to wade across
to the other side.)

1091
00:40:48,442 --> 00:40:51,136
(Unexpected underwater trekking)

1092
00:40:51,349 --> 00:40:54,217
How are we going to cross over
with all our stuff?

1093
00:40:55,118 --> 00:40:56,853
It looks pretty deep.

1094
00:40:57,921 --> 00:40:59,823
I think it comes up to your thighs.

1095
00:40:59,882 --> 00:41:01,882
Still, what do we do?

1096
00:41:02,214 --> 00:41:05,560
(For safety, the crew crosses first.)

1097
00:41:05,780 --> 00:41:08,198
They're linking arms
so they don't get swept away.

1098
00:41:09,540 --> 00:41:10,587
(Watching makes them even more nervous.)

1099
00:41:10,620 --> 00:41:12,535
Our buddies crossing the river.

1100
00:41:13,136 --> 00:41:16,139
I'm gonna get soaked anyway,
so I might as well roll it down.

1101
00:41:17,285 --> 00:41:18,875
He says it's going to be
slippery barefoot.

1102
00:41:18,965 --> 00:41:19,876
I'll be fine.

1103
00:41:19,877 --> 00:41:21,311
- You sure?
- Yeah, I'll try.

1104
00:41:21,625 --> 00:41:22,912
Okay.

1105
00:41:23,646 --> 00:41:25,381
We'll be grabbing this.

1106
00:41:25,982 --> 00:41:28,418
Okay, let's go!

1107
00:41:29,287 --> 00:41:33,223
(Won Ji carefully takes her first step.)

1108
00:41:34,726 --> 00:41:36,360
- It's cold.
- It's refreshing.

1109
00:41:36,361 --> 00:41:37,861
Ipu, you're too fast.

1110
00:41:38,396 --> 00:41:39,896
Ipu, you're too fast.

1111
00:41:41,199 --> 00:41:42,366
Ipu is too fast.

1112
00:41:45,337 --> 00:41:47,038
The current is really strong,

1113
00:41:47,039 --> 00:41:48,873
so we have to walk diagonally.

1114
00:41:50,142 --> 00:41:52,065
The current is really strong.

1115
00:41:52,298 --> 00:41:53,821
It doesn't look like it, though.

1116
00:41:53,845 --> 00:41:56,446
(She staggers if she lets her guard down.)

1117
00:41:56,748 --> 00:41:59,951
(The younger ones
slowly enter the water too.)

1118
00:42:02,687 --> 00:42:03,687
(Harimu is the only one taking it easy.)

1119
00:42:03,688 --> 00:42:04,888
It's slippery.

1120
00:42:07,559 --> 00:42:09,125
The current is really strong.

1121
00:42:09,961 --> 00:42:11,295
The current is insane.

1122
00:42:12,364 --> 00:42:13,665
(Especially hard for a paper doll,
who lacks balance)

1123
00:42:13,666 --> 00:42:14,999
I can't keep my balance.

1124
00:42:16,334 --> 00:42:21,905
(She bravely pushes
through the strong current.)

1125
00:42:22,041 --> 00:42:24,007
This is fun.

1126
00:42:24,542 --> 00:42:26,943
(The eldest gains
confidence and speeds up.)

1127
00:42:27,946 --> 00:42:29,613
(Gabee and Harimu slow down
for the frightened Sian.)

1128
00:42:29,614 --> 00:42:30,948
She's already way over there.

1129
00:42:31,349 --> 00:42:33,450
I made it. Thank you, Ipu.

1130
00:42:34,285 --> 00:42:35,285
It's so cool.

1131
00:42:36,819 --> 00:42:38,061
This is so refreshing.

1132
00:42:38,085 --> 00:42:40,023
(The younger ones are almost there too.)

1133
00:42:41,122 --> 00:42:45,863
(They safely crossed the river.)

1134
00:42:46,131 --> 00:42:47,264
We're eating here.

1135
00:42:47,799 --> 00:42:49,700
- Let's go eat.
- I'm exhausted.

1136
00:42:51,304 --> 00:42:53,437
- Harimu, do you want to get in the water?
- Yes.

1137
00:42:53,438 --> 00:42:54,705
Should we just soak our feet?

1138
00:42:54,706 --> 00:42:56,607
I wanna take this off and get in.

1139
00:42:59,344 --> 00:43:00,411
(Staggering)

1140
00:43:01,180 --> 00:43:02,613
This is like dancing too.

1141
00:43:03,481 --> 00:43:04,915
(She turns her fall into a scorpion pose.)

1142
00:43:04,916 --> 00:43:05,983
I'm dying.

1143
00:43:06,551 --> 00:43:07,518
It's so refreshing.

1144
00:43:07,952 --> 00:43:10,186
- I just want to stay here.
- Me too.

1145
00:43:10,321 --> 00:43:11,488
It's so cool.

1146
00:43:11,489 --> 00:43:12,822
(Looking around)

1147
00:43:12,823 --> 00:43:14,658
Ipu, what are you looking for?

1148
00:43:14,826 --> 00:43:15,692
A stone.

1149
00:43:16,294 --> 00:43:17,628
Another new thing.

1150
00:43:18,364 --> 00:43:19,696
He's doing something fun again.

1151
00:43:20,265 --> 00:43:21,565
I think this is mud.

1152
00:43:22,433 --> 00:43:24,334
(Ipu shows off a new trick.)

1153
00:43:24,637 --> 00:43:26,670
It really rubs off on his hand.

1154
00:43:26,671 --> 00:43:27,971
(A clay-like stone that turns into mud)

1155
00:43:28,640 --> 00:43:29,873
That's amazing.

1156
00:43:30,208 --> 00:43:31,542
It's totally like a crayon.

1157
00:43:32,510 --> 00:43:33,343
What is this?

1158
00:43:33,711 --> 00:43:34,511
A stone.

1159
00:43:34,913 --> 00:43:35,745
A stone?

1160
00:43:36,581 --> 00:43:38,658
(It is a stone, though.)

1161
00:43:38,683 --> 00:43:39,549
- A stone?
- Yes.

1162
00:43:39,550 --> 00:43:41,685
The color is so vivid.

1163
00:43:42,253 --> 00:43:43,987
(Smoothing)

1164
00:43:44,322 --> 00:43:45,756
(Ipu paints Gabee's face.)

1165
00:43:46,724 --> 00:43:49,626
(He starts decorating Gabee.)

1166
00:43:50,595 --> 00:43:53,897
(With careful touches)

1167
00:43:55,834 --> 00:43:57,466
Looks like he's just playing around.

1168
00:43:59,137 --> 00:44:01,338
(Laughing)

1169
00:44:01,673 --> 00:44:03,007
I think it's done.

1170
00:44:05,276 --> 00:44:08,345
(He even pays attention to the symmetry.)

1171
00:44:08,980 --> 00:44:10,414
Ipu did this for me.

1172
00:44:12,486 --> 00:44:14,018
(Like a fierce cat)

1173
00:44:15,787 --> 00:44:17,821
(The artist proudly admires his work.)

1174
00:44:18,256 --> 00:44:19,723
(Glancing)

1175
00:44:19,991 --> 00:44:20,857
Come here, Ipu.

1176
00:44:21,659 --> 00:44:24,628
I can write your name in Korean.
Do you want to see?

1177
00:44:25,930 --> 00:44:28,698
(Deeply focused)

1178
00:44:29,067 --> 00:44:32,069
(She carefully writes his name.)

1179
00:44:32,804 --> 00:44:34,238
- This is your name.
- Thank you.

1180
00:44:34,706 --> 00:44:36,240
Done. I like it.

1181
00:44:36,241 --> 00:44:37,641
I wrote his name on his arm.

1182
00:44:37,877 --> 00:44:39,043
That's so sweet.

1183
00:44:39,044 --> 00:44:40,244
(It's pretty, so it's fine.)

1184
00:44:40,411 --> 00:44:41,277
This might work.

1185
00:44:41,278 --> 00:44:43,246
Let's try writing Abra-ca-Empty with it.

1186
00:44:43,247 --> 00:44:44,147
"Empty."

1187
00:44:44,148 --> 00:44:45,615
(Swiping)

1188
00:44:46,484 --> 00:44:49,228
(She leaves a semi-permanent memory.)

1189
00:44:49,253 --> 00:44:50,120
This is our mark.

1190
00:44:50,989 --> 00:44:52,790
You've decorated diaries before, right?

1191
00:44:52,791 --> 00:44:53,791
Of course I have.

1192
00:44:56,995 --> 00:44:57,795
Hello.

1193
00:44:58,863 --> 00:45:00,463
Here's your lunch.

1194
00:45:00,464 --> 00:45:03,267
(Lunch is finally ready.)

1195
00:45:03,401 --> 00:45:05,635
- What's that?
- This looks so nice.

1196
00:45:06,738 --> 00:45:09,239
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

1197
00:45:09,264 --> 00:45:12,443
(Lunch is nasi goreng
topped with chicken.)

1198
00:45:13,045 --> 00:45:14,878
This is amazing.

1199
00:45:16,214 --> 00:45:17,381
Chicken.

1200
00:45:18,082 --> 00:45:20,984
(Pretty much means "thank you so much.")

1201
00:45:21,519 --> 00:45:24,054
Eating with our feet
in the water would be amazing.

1202
00:45:24,055 --> 00:45:25,655
I'd be so happy.

1203
00:45:27,125 --> 00:45:28,893
Should I sit here?

1204
00:45:28,894 --> 00:45:30,360
(She finds a suitable rock and sits.)

1205
00:45:30,828 --> 00:45:33,596
(They take a bite
as soon as they sit down.)

1206
00:45:36,067 --> 00:45:37,767
It's spicy and so good.

1207
00:45:38,603 --> 00:45:39,803
Is this nasi goreng?

1208
00:45:40,872 --> 00:45:42,239
Yes, I think so.

1209
00:45:43,541 --> 00:45:45,809
(Now, a bite of chicken)

1210
00:45:46,144 --> 00:45:47,677
The chicken is good.

1211
00:45:47,678 --> 00:45:48,645
Exactly.

1212
00:45:50,315 --> 00:45:51,882
(Excited)

1213
00:45:51,883 --> 00:45:52,850
I love this.

1214
00:45:54,118 --> 00:45:54,951
Beer.

1215
00:45:56,721 --> 00:45:57,654
Beer.

1216
00:45:57,655 --> 00:45:59,122
(The vibe makes you crave a beer.)

1217
00:45:59,123 --> 00:45:59,923
A bottle of beer.

1218
00:46:04,462 --> 00:46:07,097
There's nothing Ipu can't do.

1219
00:46:08,366 --> 00:46:09,666
He's using a piece of plastic.

1220
00:46:09,667 --> 00:46:11,601
(Making bird sounds
with a piece of plastic)

1221
00:46:12,904 --> 00:46:13,937
The sound is cute.

1222
00:46:13,938 --> 00:46:15,605
(He plays birdsong
using a piece of plastic.)

1223
00:46:16,274 --> 00:46:18,942
(They savor the chicken,
listening to artificial bird sounds.)

1224
00:46:19,310 --> 00:46:20,343
It's so delicious.

1225
00:46:20,344 --> 00:46:22,479
(Ipu wanders off somewhere again.)

1226
00:46:22,747 --> 00:46:24,848
Look at Ipu's nails.

1227
00:46:25,650 --> 00:46:27,118
He puts fake nails on his fingers.

1228
00:46:27,119 --> 00:46:28,986
- Oh, right.
- Look at that.

1229
00:46:29,621 --> 00:46:30,554
Is that real?

1230
00:46:30,955 --> 00:46:32,689
(He returns with nail extensions.)

1231
00:46:32,690 --> 00:46:35,258
- It's crazy.
- Ipu is a local here.

1232
00:46:36,294 --> 00:46:37,894
Harimu, bring it on.

1233
00:46:38,596 --> 00:46:40,230
- Harimu, bring it on.
- Why are they so long?

1234
00:46:40,231 --> 00:46:41,398
I'm seriously jealous.

1235
00:46:41,799 --> 00:46:43,700
(Ipu's nails become communal property.)

1236
00:46:45,803 --> 00:46:47,203
It's stealing our food.

1237
00:46:48,373 --> 00:46:49,273
Hey.

1238
00:46:49,707 --> 00:46:51,408
(The monkey eats and runs.)

1239
00:46:51,709 --> 00:46:52,842
It eats behind us.

1240
00:46:53,474 --> 00:46:54,713
(It snatches their food in an instant.)

1241
00:46:54,714 --> 00:46:55,679
It's cute.

1242
00:46:56,414 --> 00:46:58,181
- Amazing.
- It's eating in such a hurry.

1243
00:46:58,716 --> 00:47:00,448
They're having the time of their lives.

1244
00:47:00,449 --> 00:47:01,718
(Almost like a company dinner)

1245
00:47:01,919 --> 00:47:03,353
Monkey.

1246
00:47:03,354 --> 00:47:05,288
What are you doing? Come here.

1247
00:47:06,024 --> 00:47:08,258
(A quick monkey playtime)

1248
00:47:08,393 --> 00:47:09,893
(She plays well.)

1249
00:47:10,228 --> 00:47:12,162
Hold on.

1250
00:47:12,730 --> 00:47:14,330
Look over there.

1251
00:47:14,399 --> 00:47:16,599
(A new creature appears.)

1252
00:47:16,600 --> 00:47:17,467
A lizard?

1253
00:47:18,202 --> 00:47:21,171
- There really is a crocodile.
- It's huge.

1254
00:47:21,172 --> 00:47:22,572
It's not a crocodile, is it?

1255
00:47:22,573 --> 00:47:23,573
It's a lizard.

1256
00:47:23,574 --> 00:47:26,676
Its tongue is completely black.

1257
00:47:27,311 --> 00:47:28,845
I'm a huge fan of those.

1258
00:47:30,114 --> 00:47:31,681
It's eyeing Ipu's bag.

1259
00:47:32,650 --> 00:47:34,751
(It shows interest in Ipu's bag.)

1260
00:47:34,752 --> 00:47:35,718
No, stop.

1261
00:47:35,854 --> 00:47:37,621
Ipu's eyes have changed again.

1262
00:47:37,622 --> 00:47:39,155
(The bag owner's gaze
suddenly turns fierce.)

1263
00:47:40,375 --> 00:47:41,724
Is he hunting?

1264
00:47:43,094 --> 00:47:44,194
This is true nature.

1265
00:47:44,195 --> 00:47:45,328
(A standoff over the bag)

1266
00:47:45,830 --> 00:47:46,696
Amazing.

1267
00:47:46,697 --> 00:47:47,631
(Sneaking closer)

1268
00:47:47,632 --> 00:47:49,633
(Threatening)

1269
00:47:50,201 --> 00:47:51,701
(Flinches)

1270
00:47:51,702 --> 00:47:52,936
They're exactly alike.

1271
00:47:53,671 --> 00:47:55,303
I think Ipu's trying to catch it.

1272
00:47:56,507 --> 00:47:58,842
This is an incredibly tense standoff.

1273
00:47:59,277 --> 00:48:00,444
Between Ipu...

1274
00:48:00,778 --> 00:48:02,479
(Thrilling)

1275
00:48:03,014 --> 00:48:04,081
And the lizard.

1276
00:48:04,082 --> 00:48:05,115
(He approaches at its eye level.)

1277
00:48:05,116 --> 00:48:06,583
I think he's going to catch it.

1278
00:48:06,584 --> 00:48:07,317
(Dashing)

1279
00:48:07,719 --> 00:48:09,886
(The water monitor briefly retreats.)

1280
00:48:10,388 --> 00:48:11,922
(He chases it fiercely.)

1281
00:48:12,223 --> 00:48:13,390
(Is it retreating for good?)

1282
00:48:13,391 --> 00:48:14,191
(Swishes around)

1283
00:48:17,361 --> 00:48:19,229
(Chaos)

1284
00:48:19,831 --> 00:48:22,132
(It charges straight
at the two biggest scaredy-cats.)

1285
00:48:22,900 --> 00:48:25,703
(It makes a beeline for the river.)

1286
00:48:25,704 --> 00:48:26,770
It's amazing.

1287
00:48:27,105 --> 00:48:28,238
It's insane.

1288
00:48:29,707 --> 00:48:31,041
(An undignified exit)

1289
00:48:31,042 --> 00:48:32,674
It's funny how it
suddenly started swimming.

1290
00:48:33,878 --> 00:48:34,845
Pure nature.

1291
00:48:36,614 --> 00:48:40,417
I'd get to see a real lizard
in the wild for the first time.

1292
00:48:40,818 --> 00:48:43,019
It'd be so scary if they came out
while we're sleeping.

1293
00:48:43,020 --> 00:48:44,921
- Oh, no.
- They might come out at night.

1294
00:48:44,956 --> 00:48:46,490
I should hug my bag while I sleep.

1295
00:48:46,624 --> 00:48:48,758
I won't be able to sleep tonight.

1296
00:48:48,960 --> 00:48:49,760
Okay.

1297
00:48:50,027 --> 00:48:51,394
We're heading to the campsite now.

1298
00:48:51,629 --> 00:48:53,863
- Okay.
- Finally.

1299
00:48:53,931 --> 00:48:54,697
It takes two hours.

1300
00:48:54,698 --> 00:48:56,232
- Don't lie.
- Don't lie.

1301
00:48:56,233 --> 00:48:58,167
(The cry-wolf uncle
keeps going without a care.)

1302
00:48:58,168 --> 00:48:59,168
Okay, let's go.

1303
00:48:59,169 --> 00:48:59,969
- Okay.
- Let's go.

1304
00:48:59,970 --> 00:49:01,738
Let's see.

1305
00:49:02,006 --> 00:49:04,674
Let's see if it really takes two hours.

1306
00:49:04,943 --> 00:49:07,243
So far, we've been in the mountains.

1307
00:49:08,079 --> 00:49:10,781
Now it's starting to feel like a jungle.

1308
00:49:12,850 --> 00:49:15,185
There are so many more weeds.

1309
00:49:15,920 --> 00:49:18,088
It's getting more and more jungle-like.

1310
00:49:18,089 --> 00:49:19,289
It really feels like a jungle.

1311
00:49:19,724 --> 00:49:22,526
There seem to be lots of plants
you'd find in a jungle.

1312
00:49:22,530 --> 00:49:23,456
Right.

1313
00:49:24,228 --> 00:49:27,163
It looks like nature is
really well preserved here.

1314
00:49:27,499 --> 00:49:28,932
- I love it.
- I love it too.

1315
00:49:30,002 --> 00:49:33,704
It's much denser,
and the path has gotten really narrow.

1316
00:49:36,140 --> 00:49:38,908
I feel like I've come to a new planet.

1317
00:49:39,811 --> 00:49:40,944
It's awesome.

1318
00:49:40,945 --> 00:49:44,281
(Deeper and deeper into the jungle)

1319
00:49:44,782 --> 00:49:46,748
What are we doing
when we get to the campsite?

1320
00:49:47,251 --> 00:49:49,219
- Ipu.
- Yes.

1321
00:49:49,453 --> 00:49:50,453
Do we have a schedule?

1322
00:49:50,955 --> 00:49:52,354
- Nothing.
- Nothing?

1323
00:49:52,857 --> 00:49:54,057
Nothing today.

1324
00:49:54,058 --> 00:49:55,425
(Yay, free time)

1325
00:49:55,560 --> 00:49:57,494
Nice. Let's swim and play.

1326
00:49:58,096 --> 00:50:00,163
We definitely have to swim here.

1327
00:50:01,265 --> 00:50:03,032
(He spots something.)

1328
00:50:03,667 --> 00:50:06,075
What's that?

1329
00:50:06,415 --> 00:50:07,604
Is that the nail?

1330
00:50:07,605 --> 00:50:08,838
(Those nails from the stream)

1331
00:50:09,006 --> 00:50:10,506
Harimu, are you nervous?

1332
00:50:11,642 --> 00:50:12,875
- No.
- Are you?

1333
00:50:13,211 --> 00:50:13,977
No.

1334
00:50:14,745 --> 00:50:17,714
They look like they're
five times longer than your nails.

1335
00:50:17,849 --> 00:50:18,849
I know.

1336
00:50:18,850 --> 00:50:20,484
Isn't he making them too long?

1337
00:50:20,485 --> 00:50:23,086
I've never seen anyone
with longer nails than yours.

1338
00:50:23,087 --> 00:50:24,521
Natural nails.

1339
00:50:24,522 --> 00:50:26,523
(A slight sense of danger)

1340
00:50:26,657 --> 00:50:28,291
He's making them way too long.

1341
00:50:28,960 --> 00:50:29,960
(Challenge)

1342
00:50:30,428 --> 00:50:31,461
(How dare you.)

1343
00:50:33,698 --> 00:50:34,765
(Staggering)

1344
00:50:34,832 --> 00:50:35,966
(Queen Ipu's legs give out.)

1345
00:50:35,967 --> 00:50:36,733
Sorry.

1346
00:50:38,202 --> 00:50:40,637
- Oh, my.
- He's so charming.

1347
00:50:41,138 --> 00:50:42,305
Ipu is so charming.

1348
00:50:42,306 --> 00:50:43,573
(Ipu is acting cute.)

1349
00:50:43,774 --> 00:50:45,508
You're so funny.

1350
00:50:45,710 --> 00:50:46,777
You're very funny.

1351
00:50:46,778 --> 00:50:48,679
But it's so fun that everything here is...

1352
00:50:48,946 --> 00:50:51,214
basically his toy and his playground.

1353
00:50:51,215 --> 00:50:53,116
Exactly. That's so Ipu.

1354
00:50:54,919 --> 00:50:56,987
There's an even more
amazing spot over there.

1355
00:50:58,556 --> 00:51:00,423
There's someone over there too.

1356
00:51:01,392 --> 00:51:03,092
We're not crossing over there, are we?

1357
00:51:03,995 --> 00:51:05,261
Is that our campsite?

1358
00:51:06,297 --> 00:51:08,698
Is that our campsite?

1359
00:51:09,333 --> 00:51:10,233
Yes, that's it.

1360
00:51:10,835 --> 00:51:11,936
- Over there.
- Really?

1361
00:51:12,803 --> 00:51:15,238
(The campsite is across the stream.)

1362
00:51:15,239 --> 00:51:16,773
(Their second crossing already)

1363
00:51:17,408 --> 00:51:18,975
We're going.

1364
00:51:19,377 --> 00:51:20,277
It's refreshing.

1365
00:51:21,045 --> 00:51:22,879
This looks like it'll be the deepest one.

1366
00:51:23,848 --> 00:51:26,583
It's deep.

1367
00:51:27,157 --> 00:51:29,157
The current is really strong.

1368
00:51:32,689 --> 00:51:33,524
It's nice.

1369
00:51:33,722 --> 00:51:34,992
It's a funny life.

1370
00:51:35,155 --> 00:51:36,394
It's a very good life.

1371
00:51:37,609 --> 00:51:38,662
It's refreshing.

1372
00:51:41,107 --> 00:51:42,299
Are you all right?

1373
00:51:42,393 --> 00:51:43,300
Yes.

1374
00:51:43,447 --> 00:51:44,969
I'm so all right.

1375
00:51:46,883 --> 00:51:49,182
- Nice.
- It's refreshing.

1376
00:51:49,207 --> 00:51:52,038
(The cool water washes away all the heat.)

1377
00:51:55,424 --> 00:51:56,447
Thank you.

1378
00:51:56,484 --> 00:51:59,116
Thank you, Ipu.

1379
00:51:59,138 --> 00:52:00,184
(Ipu, thanks.)

1380
00:52:00,684 --> 00:52:02,684
(They finally crossed the river.)

1381
00:52:02,685 --> 00:52:04,937
It's so nice.

1382
00:52:05,098 --> 00:52:06,724
They're swimming over there.

1383
00:52:07,458 --> 00:52:08,826
Let's swim later too.

1384
00:52:09,031 --> 00:52:10,628
Here?

1385
00:52:11,338 --> 00:52:13,130
Is that our campsite?

1386
00:52:13,305 --> 00:52:15,305
You said we had two more hours to go.
You're a liar.

1387
00:52:15,585 --> 00:52:16,934
- Two minutes.
- Two minutes.

1388
00:52:16,935 --> 00:52:19,136
- Yes!
- Finally, only two minutes.

1389
00:52:19,445 --> 00:52:21,939
- Jungle!
- Welcome to the Jungle.

1390
00:52:21,940 --> 00:52:24,020
(As soon as we walk in,
they see an old, rundown hut.)

1391
00:52:24,720 --> 00:52:25,943
No way. Wait.

1392
00:52:26,444 --> 00:52:27,578
Hold on.

1393
00:52:28,879 --> 00:52:31,348
- I can't believe it.
- Those are bamboo houses.

1394
00:52:32,139 --> 00:52:34,351
Please. This is a lie.

1395
00:52:34,352 --> 00:52:35,332
(Flustered)

1396
00:52:35,492 --> 00:52:37,766
(Staggering)

1397
00:52:37,799 --> 00:52:40,491
How do people even find a place like this?

1398
00:52:41,959 --> 00:52:43,561
Seriously, this is legendary.

1399
00:52:43,562 --> 00:52:44,772
(Today's lodging is Eco-friendly.)

1400
00:52:45,678 --> 00:52:49,478
(About a four-hour trek to get here)

1401
00:52:49,834 --> 00:52:52,503
This is pretty much
an indigenous experience.

1402
00:52:53,904 --> 00:52:56,607
I should've brought just one outfit.

1403
00:52:56,608 --> 00:53:01,371
(It took them eight hours
to get here from Medan.)

1404
00:53:01,438 --> 00:53:03,981
It's just divided into different spaces.

1405
00:53:03,982 --> 00:53:06,317
It's really well built with bamboo.

1406
00:53:06,415 --> 00:53:08,919
It's totally a bamboo house.

1407
00:53:09,522 --> 00:53:11,082
What is that?

1408
00:53:11,962 --> 00:53:15,815
(Orangutans show up here all the time.)

1409
00:53:15,941 --> 00:53:21,535
(This jungle lodge coexists
with the wildlife.)

1410
00:53:21,941 --> 00:53:25,202
There are so many houses here.

1411
00:53:26,052 --> 00:53:27,571
Where's our home?

1412
00:53:29,894 --> 00:53:31,542
- The blue one.
- The blue one.

1413
00:53:32,042 --> 00:53:33,177
That must be it.

1414
00:53:33,644 --> 00:53:34,712
Let's go.

1415
00:53:35,613 --> 00:53:36,947
Let's check it out.

1416
00:53:37,473 --> 00:53:38,782
This is it.

1417
00:53:40,606 --> 00:53:41,719
This is your room.

1418
00:53:43,666 --> 00:53:45,946
(Arriving at their lodging
eight hours after leaving their hotel)

1419
00:53:45,947 --> 00:53:46,991
A room tour.

1420
00:53:47,553 --> 00:53:48,392
What?

1421
00:53:50,279 --> 00:53:51,962
That's unbelievable.

1422
00:53:53,464 --> 00:53:54,932
- How can it be like this?
- Gosh.

1423
00:53:56,033 --> 00:53:57,687
I've never slept in a place like this.

1424
00:53:57,721 --> 00:53:58,869
How is this possible?

1425
00:54:00,128 --> 00:54:02,988
(Here's today's lodging.)

1426
00:54:04,628 --> 00:54:07,766
(You can see the entire interior
at a glance.)

1427
00:54:08,912 --> 00:54:11,606
(An ultra-minimalist lodge)

1428
00:54:11,666 --> 00:54:12,950
There's our backpack!

1429
00:54:13,126 --> 00:54:14,919
Our backpack is here.

1430
00:54:15,825 --> 00:54:16,720
This is insane.

1431
00:54:16,721 --> 00:54:19,056
Let us take a look around our room.

1432
00:54:19,086 --> 00:54:20,057
A room tour.

1433
00:54:20,412 --> 00:54:21,859
Room One.

1434
00:54:21,860 --> 00:54:23,327
Room Two.

1435
00:54:24,193 --> 00:54:25,663
Room Three.

1436
00:54:26,263 --> 00:54:27,765
Room Four.

1437
00:54:28,507 --> 00:54:30,333
And...

1438
00:54:30,568 --> 00:54:32,469
there are no windows.

1439
00:54:32,470 --> 00:54:34,114
(This room feels insanely open.)

1440
00:54:34,294 --> 00:54:36,294
The mosquito net has a hole in it.

1441
00:54:36,728 --> 00:54:38,861
(Stunned)

1442
00:54:39,341 --> 00:54:40,574
- Do you like it?
- It's good!

1443
00:54:40,575 --> 00:54:42,646
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1444
00:54:42,829 --> 00:54:44,182
There's no electricity.

1445
00:54:44,235 --> 00:54:46,235
- No electricity?
- No.

1446
00:54:46,750 --> 00:54:47,985
- No lights either?
- Yes.

1447
00:54:48,049 --> 00:54:49,253
Okay.

1448
00:54:49,881 --> 00:54:51,254
- You're right.
- There's nothing here.

1449
00:54:51,255 --> 00:54:52,315
You don't get a signal here either.

1450
00:54:52,316 --> 00:54:54,316
We should rely on our video light.

1451
00:54:55,008 --> 00:54:58,215
If you want to make a call,
climb up a tree.

1452
00:54:58,216 --> 00:54:59,328
Okay.

1453
00:55:00,331 --> 00:55:02,499
If we get bored, let's climb a tree.

1454
00:55:03,428 --> 00:55:04,702
(Losing her mind)

1455
00:55:04,828 --> 00:55:06,828
This is so romantic.

1456
00:55:07,488 --> 00:55:09,540
Oh, my. This is nice.

1457
00:55:10,135 --> 00:55:11,375
Yes.

1458
00:55:11,702 --> 00:55:14,046
(Laughing)

1459
00:55:14,216 --> 00:55:16,656
I wish nighttime would never come
and it could just stay like this all day.

1460
00:55:16,681 --> 00:55:18,749
- Wouldn't it be scary at night?
- I think so too.

1461
00:55:18,750 --> 00:55:20,884
We might hear a lot of animals at night.

1462
00:55:21,346 --> 00:55:24,555
There are no doors. It's all open.

1463
00:55:24,804 --> 00:55:27,377
Monkeys can come in and take something
while we're sleeping.

1464
00:55:27,378 --> 00:55:28,359
We should be careful.

1465
00:55:28,897 --> 00:55:32,191
(Orangutans also pop up
from time to time.)

1466
00:55:32,884 --> 00:55:35,409
(They roam freely through the trees...)

1467
00:55:36,175 --> 00:55:40,129
(and all around the area.)

1468
00:55:42,909 --> 00:55:45,522
(Take good care of your backpack.)

1469
00:55:45,689 --> 00:55:48,227
- How about snakes?
- Even if you see them, that's fine.

1470
00:55:48,387 --> 00:55:50,660
Just put them in your mouths.

1471
00:55:51,213 --> 00:55:53,150
Is that everything?

1472
00:55:53,550 --> 00:55:55,225
- It's here.
- Where?

1473
00:55:55,226 --> 00:55:57,154
This is everything.

1474
00:55:57,226 --> 00:55:59,013
- All we have is one backpack.
- One bag.

1475
00:55:59,014 --> 00:56:00,224
We're compact.

1476
00:56:00,253 --> 00:56:01,352
One bag for four people.

1477
00:56:01,353 --> 00:56:03,327
You have one bag for yourself.

1478
00:56:03,346 --> 00:56:04,962
- Why?
- Why?

1479
00:56:04,993 --> 00:56:06,079
I don't know.

1480
00:56:06,139 --> 00:56:07,298
Ask him.

1481
00:56:08,346 --> 00:56:09,299
Hello.

1482
00:56:10,246 --> 00:56:12,346
Why do they share one bag?

1483
00:56:12,719 --> 00:56:14,159
(Satisfying)

1484
00:56:14,192 --> 00:56:16,205
- Excuse me.
- Why?

1485
00:56:16,206 --> 00:56:19,243
Even Ipu is asking why.
He finds it strange too.

1486
00:56:19,339 --> 00:56:21,545
Even though he feels at home in nature.

1487
00:56:21,592 --> 00:56:22,713
Not enough.

1488
00:56:22,714 --> 00:56:24,148
Right. It's not enough.

1489
00:56:25,444 --> 00:56:28,252
Even the nature man has one bag.

1490
00:56:29,039 --> 00:56:31,592
(They're more minimalist
than someone living in nature.)

1491
00:56:31,826 --> 00:56:33,590
I'm so sweaty, I want to get in the water.

1492
00:56:33,924 --> 00:56:35,459
Let's go for a swim.

1493
00:56:35,692 --> 00:56:36,966
Let's shower there.

1494
00:56:36,967 --> 00:56:38,128
- Okay.
- Really?

1495
00:56:38,306 --> 00:56:39,298
- Let's go.
- Sounds good.

1496
00:56:39,352 --> 00:56:41,699
- Right away.
- Go now.

1497
00:56:42,239 --> 00:56:43,279
What did you say?

1498
00:56:43,352 --> 00:56:44,535
- "Go now."
- "Go now."

1499
00:56:44,586 --> 00:56:46,432
We're just saying, "Let's go."

1500
00:56:46,459 --> 00:56:48,639
- Let's go. Go now.
- Go now.

1501
00:56:48,966 --> 00:56:50,217
(He learned quickly.)

1502
00:56:51,308 --> 00:56:53,377
<i>Go now</i>

1503
00:56:54,337 --> 00:56:57,483
(Today's shower spot is the river
they just crossed.)

1504
00:56:57,496 --> 00:56:59,883
- Gosh!
- We're here.

1505
00:57:00,284 --> 00:57:01,652
Let's go in.

1506
00:57:04,788 --> 00:57:06,924
The water looks blue.

1507
00:57:07,424 --> 00:57:09,560
Let's take our shoes off and jump in!

1508
00:57:09,893 --> 00:57:10,961
Let's go!

1509
00:57:11,055 --> 00:57:12,329
- Let's go!
- Bamboo!

1510
00:57:12,330 --> 00:57:14,098
What is that? I want to ride on that.

1511
00:57:14,223 --> 00:57:15,499
What is that?

1512
00:57:15,590 --> 00:57:18,102
- Awesome.
- That's cool.

1513
00:57:18,257 --> 00:57:20,257
It's refreshing.

1514
00:57:20,504 --> 00:57:21,739
I'm going in.

1515
00:57:22,277 --> 00:57:24,343
(Getting ready to get in the water)

1516
00:57:25,863 --> 00:57:30,350
(Running into the water)

1517
00:57:30,570 --> 00:57:31,815
Wait. I'm drifting away.

1518
00:57:33,799 --> 00:57:35,452
(A cold shower)

1519
00:57:35,453 --> 00:57:37,367
- I'm drifting away.
- It's carrying me away.

1520
00:57:37,392 --> 00:57:39,547
- Goodbye!
- Goodbye!

1521
00:57:40,141 --> 00:57:42,593
We're throwing off all the shackles
of the world,

1522
00:57:42,794 --> 00:57:45,729
and heading back to Korea.

1523
00:57:47,297 --> 00:57:49,266
There's a monkey over there.

1524
00:57:49,471 --> 00:57:50,501
Where?

1525
00:57:50,544 --> 00:57:51,902
It stopped.

1526
00:57:51,903 --> 00:57:53,551
(There are monkeys everywhere you look.)

1527
00:57:54,004 --> 00:57:55,305
Your butt.

1528
00:57:55,939 --> 00:57:57,574
Your butt looks huge.

1529
00:57:59,224 --> 00:58:01,931
(Her butt is filled with air.)

1530
00:58:02,778 --> 00:58:04,398
You're farting.

1531
00:58:06,551 --> 00:58:10,055
(Splashing around
with just their faces above the surface)

1532
00:58:10,389 --> 00:58:12,389
Harimu is here.

1533
00:58:12,449 --> 00:58:14,191
Harimu, come on in.

1534
00:58:14,192 --> 00:58:16,055
- I'm back.
- Come on.

1535
00:58:20,333 --> 00:58:24,120
(Playing and showering at the same time)

1536
00:58:24,984 --> 00:58:28,158
Her waacking is crazy.

1537
00:58:28,578 --> 00:58:29,884
(Twerking)

1538
00:58:30,464 --> 00:58:32,378
(A new skill, twerking in the water!)

1539
00:58:33,038 --> 00:58:35,629
(Twerking for the members again)

1540
00:58:36,202 --> 00:58:39,668
(Satisfied)

1541
00:58:39,669 --> 00:58:40,684
That's so funny.

1542
00:58:40,702 --> 00:58:42,986
Is it okay to wash your hair
with just water?

1543
00:58:43,196 --> 00:58:44,321
I think so.

1544
00:58:44,621 --> 00:58:46,056
It's super cold.

1545
00:58:47,434 --> 00:58:49,493
It's waking me up. My brain!

1546
00:58:49,700 --> 00:58:50,847
I can feel my brain.

1547
00:58:51,174 --> 00:58:52,634
- It's so cold.
- I can feel my brain.

1548
00:58:52,635 --> 00:58:55,647
- I can really feel my brain.
- Let me wash your hair.

1549
00:58:56,120 --> 00:58:58,368
- My brain feels alive.
- Let me massage your head.

1550
00:59:01,014 --> 00:59:02,706
It's so refreshing.

1551
00:59:04,120 --> 00:59:05,542
Ma'am.

1552
00:59:05,543 --> 00:59:07,820
Let me give you a head massage.

1553
00:59:08,066 --> 00:59:10,514
- A head massage for you too.
- Thank you.

1554
00:59:10,926 --> 00:59:12,806
(The water is nice, and Sian is kind.)

1555
00:59:12,840 --> 00:59:14,651
I feel so free.

1556
00:59:14,673 --> 00:59:17,421
- This is paradise.
- Really.

1557
00:59:18,989 --> 00:59:22,326
Then you get up and see nature.

1558
00:59:22,826 --> 00:59:24,461
You can see nature in every direction.

1559
00:59:24,761 --> 00:59:27,564
- Nature on the side too.
- The view is stunning.

1560
00:59:27,565 --> 00:59:28,899
The perfect view for a mountain spirit.

1561
00:59:30,681 --> 00:59:32,002
Aren't we like fairies now?

1562
00:59:32,903 --> 00:59:34,471
I'll wash this too.

1563
00:59:35,072 --> 00:59:37,425
Woodcutter! Don't steal my clothes.

1564
00:59:37,426 --> 00:59:40,244
- You're watching us!
- Woodcutter!

1565
00:59:40,352 --> 00:59:41,612
Don't steal my clothes.

1566
00:59:41,613 --> 00:59:44,114
- You're so mean.
- Okay?

1567
00:59:44,210 --> 00:59:47,184
- Even if you like me, don't steal it.
- Don't steal it.

1568
00:59:48,570 --> 00:59:50,777
What's the purpose of this swimming?

1569
00:59:50,804 --> 00:59:51,955
Don't steal it.

1570
00:59:52,656 --> 00:59:54,458
We've become nature people.

1571
00:59:56,441 --> 00:59:58,668
(Scooping)

1572
00:59:58,983 --> 01:00:00,097
It's really refreshing.

1573
01:00:00,777 --> 01:00:02,966
Harimu washes her face
in an interesting way.

1574
01:00:04,201 --> 01:00:06,931
(The queen doesn't lower her head
to wash her face.)

1575
01:00:07,177 --> 01:00:10,211
(Standing)

1576
01:00:12,698 --> 01:00:15,078
- It's so nice.
- It's refreshing.

1577
01:00:15,812 --> 01:00:17,837
I feel like I'm at an outdoor hot spring.

1578
01:00:18,268 --> 01:00:19,550
A cold spring.

1579
01:00:19,918 --> 01:00:21,318
A cold spring?

1580
01:00:22,052 --> 01:00:24,078
- It looks good. What is it?
- I don't know what it is.

1581
01:00:24,079 --> 01:00:25,222
Let's sit down and eat.

1582
01:00:25,272 --> 01:00:26,557
Okay.

1583
01:00:27,357 --> 01:00:28,258
Hey!

1584
01:00:28,859 --> 01:00:29,993
Hey!

1585
01:00:32,939 --> 01:00:34,598
- Hey!
- It stole our food.

1586
01:00:34,646 --> 01:00:35,799
Hey!

1587
01:00:36,032 --> 01:00:37,401
Hey, that's mine!

1588
01:00:37,612 --> 01:00:39,519
- Gosh.
- That was mine!

1589
01:00:39,546 --> 01:00:41,905
- Give it back!
- What did it take?

1590
01:00:42,039 --> 01:00:43,252
Our food.

1591
01:00:43,492 --> 01:00:45,492
It wasn't scared at all.

1592
01:00:46,266 --> 01:00:47,939
(Collecting)

1593
01:00:47,966 --> 01:00:49,780
They just eat everything.

1594
01:00:49,965 --> 01:00:51,074
- They're not picky.
- We have one more.

1595
01:00:51,415 --> 01:00:54,014
- What is this?
- Fried sweet potato?

1596
01:00:54,015 --> 01:00:55,248
(Trying the snack later than the monkey)

1597
01:00:55,501 --> 01:00:57,187
Let me pour it.

1598
01:00:57,921 --> 01:01:00,891
- It reminds me of makgeolli.
- Right.

1599
01:01:02,002 --> 01:01:04,094
- A cup of tea?
- It's coffee.

1600
01:01:04,661 --> 01:01:06,063
A warm coffee.

1601
01:01:06,088 --> 01:01:07,965
You need hot coffee at a time like this.

1602
01:01:07,995 --> 01:01:10,582
I usually prefer iced coffee,
but I want hot coffee now.

1603
01:01:10,583 --> 01:01:13,437
Wait. We have sugar here.

1604
01:01:14,099 --> 01:01:15,672
You can add it if you want.

1605
01:01:16,740 --> 01:01:19,232
- If you like coffee, add some.
- Yes.

1606
01:01:19,786 --> 01:01:21,411
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

1607
01:01:22,619 --> 01:01:25,097
(Slurping)

1608
01:01:25,317 --> 01:01:26,617
It's good.

1609
01:01:26,831 --> 01:01:27,931
(Slurping)

1610
01:01:28,151 --> 01:01:29,785
Wow.

1611
01:01:30,120 --> 01:01:32,188
I think this coffee's
naturally a little sweet.

1612
01:01:32,189 --> 01:01:34,723
Yeah. I love it.

1613
01:01:34,958 --> 01:01:36,825
- It's a bit toasty.
- It tastes just like scorched rice.

1614
01:01:36,826 --> 01:01:37,860
It's so good.

1615
01:01:38,095 --> 01:01:38,928
What's this?

1616
01:01:39,129 --> 01:01:40,196
Shall we try this?

1617
01:01:40,831 --> 01:01:41,831
Fried bananas?

1618
01:01:42,466 --> 01:01:46,002
(Trying it immediately.)

1619
01:01:46,103 --> 01:01:47,737
Fried sweet potatoes!
Fried sweet pumpkins!

1620
01:01:47,738 --> 01:01:48,471
- Sweet pumpkins?
- Sweet potatoes!

1621
01:01:48,472 --> 01:01:49,372
It's so good.

1622
01:01:50,607 --> 01:01:51,640
It tastes like fries.

1623
01:01:51,641 --> 01:01:52,541
Wow!

1624
01:01:52,542 --> 01:01:53,676
- It's good, right?
- So crunchy.

1625
01:01:54,912 --> 01:01:56,179
It's sweet and savory.

1626
01:01:59,683 --> 01:02:00,916
They seasoned it.

1627
01:02:01,118 --> 01:02:02,185
Mmm!

1628
01:02:02,186 --> 01:02:03,219
It's so good.

1629
01:02:03,620 --> 01:02:04,486
Yeah.

1630
01:02:05,022 --> 01:02:06,656
I can see why the monkeys took it.

1631
01:02:07,724 --> 01:02:09,224
Something even monkeys want.

1632
01:02:09,660 --> 01:02:10,826
- They took a lot.
- Like four.

1633
01:02:10,827 --> 01:02:12,161
Four or six, I think.

1634
01:02:12,162 --> 01:02:13,062
- So greedy.
- They took a lot.

1635
01:02:13,063 --> 01:02:13,863
(A warm treat even the monkeys
can't resist.)

1636
01:02:14,064 --> 01:02:16,132
We have nothing to do now.

1637
01:02:16,133 --> 01:02:17,433
Our phones have no connection.

1638
01:02:18,168 --> 01:02:20,803
When it gets dark,
we won't even have that.

1639
01:02:20,804 --> 01:02:22,404
- Lamps.
- No lights.

1640
01:02:22,405 --> 01:02:23,572
- What do we do now?
- Oh, no.

1641
01:02:24,341 --> 01:02:26,075
We really have nothing to do.

1642
01:02:26,510 --> 01:02:27,809
(Staring)

1643
01:02:27,810 --> 01:02:30,780
You guys totally look like a hiking club.

1644
01:02:31,548 --> 01:02:34,316
This would be perfect for a dating show.

1645
01:02:34,317 --> 01:02:35,551
No. 1, 2, 3, 4.

1646
01:02:35,552 --> 01:02:36,819
Then...

1647
01:02:36,954 --> 01:02:38,354
We've got nothing else to do.

1648
01:02:38,355 --> 01:02:39,689
So let's film a dating show.

1649
01:02:39,923 --> 01:02:42,358
We've got five ladies and five gents here.

1650
01:02:42,359 --> 01:02:43,357
Damn.

1651
01:02:43,358 --> 01:02:46,462
Let's be honest. Is there anyone here...

1652
01:02:46,463 --> 01:02:48,264
getting a little boost from anyone?

1653
01:02:51,234 --> 01:02:54,369
Is anyone making this journey
a little easier?

1654
01:02:54,370 --> 01:02:55,470
(And no one found their motivation.)

1655
01:02:55,471 --> 01:02:56,343
Hands up!

1656
01:02:57,541 --> 01:02:59,242
Nothing gives me a dopamine rush
like romance.

1657
01:02:59,243 --> 01:03:01,177
- A show within a show.
- Yeah.

1658
01:03:01,178 --> 01:03:02,545
(An evening in the jungle
with no electricity or dopamine.)

1659
01:03:02,779 --> 01:03:05,280
As soon as we get down tomorrow,
I'm heading straight to the laundromat.

1660
01:03:05,281 --> 01:03:09,218
(Hanging wet clothes.)

1661
01:03:09,786 --> 01:03:10,953
Are you heading to that table?

1662
01:03:11,355 --> 01:03:12,522
Are you getting closer?

1663
01:03:12,789 --> 01:03:13,923
Are you sitting there?

1664
01:03:13,924 --> 01:03:16,291
Are you going for her?

1665
01:03:16,292 --> 01:03:19,628
(Squeezing dopamine)

1666
01:03:20,464 --> 01:03:23,566
(Happy)

1667
01:03:24,601 --> 01:03:30,839
(They chat away until sunset.)

1668
01:03:31,742 --> 01:03:34,344
(Meanwhile, Ipu is preparing
something for them.)

1669
01:03:35,245 --> 01:03:38,914
(Handmade from jungle wood)

1670
01:03:39,316 --> 01:03:41,384
(Crackle)

1671
01:03:42,119 --> 01:03:43,553
Ooh, a campfire.

1672
01:03:43,820 --> 01:03:44,620
Now that's a fire!

1673
01:03:44,621 --> 01:03:45,654
(Ipu's cozy campfire)

1674
01:03:45,655 --> 01:03:47,556
Wow, that fire's really roaring.

1675
01:03:47,557 --> 01:03:48,957
You can hear it roaring.

1676
01:03:49,926 --> 01:03:51,326
- This feels nice.
- So nice.

1677
01:03:52,062 --> 01:03:53,162
I love this vibe.

1678
01:03:53,163 --> 01:03:57,333
Campfire show.

1679
01:03:57,334 --> 01:03:58,434
(The fire burns bright as night falls.)

1680
01:03:59,536 --> 01:04:01,904
What was the highlight of the day
for everyone?

1681
01:04:01,905 --> 01:04:04,173
I honestly thought...

1682
01:04:04,174 --> 01:04:05,841
I'd be drenched in sweat.

1683
01:04:05,842 --> 01:04:07,510
But the weather was surprisingly nice.

1684
01:04:07,511 --> 01:04:10,713
- It was a healing course.
- I agree.

1685
01:04:10,714 --> 01:04:11,680
(Beautiful weather made the trek
all the more relaxing.)

1686
01:04:11,715 --> 01:04:13,849
Ipu was...

1687
01:04:13,850 --> 01:04:16,285
such a perfect guide.

1688
01:04:16,286 --> 01:04:17,353
Totally.

1689
01:04:17,554 --> 01:04:19,922
When Ipu first came to us and said,

1690
01:04:20,323 --> 01:04:21,757
"Let's go to the jungle."

1691
01:04:22,159 --> 01:04:23,559
That moment.

1692
01:04:23,927 --> 01:04:25,728
And the moment he said
we'd be sleeping in there.

1693
01:04:25,729 --> 01:04:26,630
- We were like, what?
- What?

1694
01:04:27,764 --> 01:04:30,366
(During today's breakfast)

1695
01:04:30,467 --> 01:04:32,668
Let me explain a little about the jungle.

1696
01:04:33,637 --> 01:04:35,538
Wow!

1697
01:04:36,406 --> 01:04:37,806
(We didn't think we'd go to a jungle.)

1698
01:04:38,175 --> 01:04:40,743
- That was a terrifying moment.
- Yeah.

1699
01:04:40,744 --> 01:04:42,311
Seriously, why are we even here?

1700
01:04:42,779 --> 01:04:45,414
After having such a nice breakfast
at the resort this morning.

1701
01:04:45,415 --> 01:04:47,516
I know, right? That place was fire.

1702
01:04:48,351 --> 01:04:49,151
It's dinner!

1703
01:04:49,453 --> 01:04:50,486
(Turning)

1704
01:04:51,188 --> 01:04:53,189
(And just in time, dinner is served.)

1705
01:04:53,190 --> 01:04:54,190
Dinner time!

1706
01:04:54,658 --> 01:04:55,658
It looks so good!

1707
01:04:56,059 --> 01:04:58,060
(Can't help but clap.)

1708
01:04:59,062 --> 01:05:01,096
It's full Indonesian style.

1709
01:05:01,198 --> 01:05:02,865
How did they even cook all this?

1710
01:05:03,867 --> 01:05:04,867
Curry!

1711
01:05:05,936 --> 01:05:07,536
Wow, these look amazing.

1712
01:05:07,537 --> 01:05:09,939
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1713
01:05:10,674 --> 01:05:12,041
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

1714
01:05:12,042 --> 01:05:14,010
(The full dinner spread is ready.)

1715
01:05:14,011 --> 01:05:16,012
I'm going for curry.

1716
01:05:16,247 --> 01:05:18,180
I love curry.

1717
01:05:18,181 --> 01:05:19,481
(Won Ji goes for curry first.)

1718
01:05:19,816 --> 01:05:21,417
This curry's really thin.

1719
01:05:21,418 --> 01:05:22,985
Yeah, it's very soupy.

1720
01:05:22,986 --> 01:05:23,986
(Almost like soup)

1721
01:05:24,588 --> 01:05:26,756
(Mix it all up.)

1722
01:05:27,524 --> 01:05:29,859
(And dig right in.)

1723
01:05:29,860 --> 01:05:31,861
(Another bite)

1724
01:05:32,129 --> 01:05:35,198
As a curry lover, how's Indonesian curry?

1725
01:05:35,199 --> 01:05:37,300
It's not as curry-like.

1726
01:05:37,301 --> 01:05:40,069
It's got a hint of curry.

1727
01:05:40,737 --> 01:05:42,738
But it's pretty thin
and really heavy on the spices.

1728
01:05:44,441 --> 01:05:45,307
It's good.

1729
01:05:47,043 --> 01:05:48,543
This looks good too. What is it?

1730
01:05:48,544 --> 01:05:50,045
I think it's like braised chicken.

1731
01:05:51,648 --> 01:05:53,282
(Nom)

1732
01:05:54,317 --> 01:05:55,117
Mmm.

1733
01:05:55,118 --> 01:05:56,184
This is so good!

1734
01:05:56,185 --> 01:05:57,085
- Is it good?
- Yes.

1735
01:05:57,255 --> 01:05:58,521
Are you talking about this one?

1736
01:05:58,688 --> 01:05:59,621
Okay.

1737
01:05:59,622 --> 01:06:01,123
(Savory chicken, stir-fried with spices.)

1738
01:06:01,391 --> 01:06:02,891
Let me try some.

1739
01:06:03,260 --> 01:06:04,994
(Nom)

1740
01:06:04,995 --> 01:06:07,563
It's like an Indonesian version
of spicy braised chicken.

1741
01:06:07,564 --> 01:06:08,497
(You're right.)

1742
01:06:08,498 --> 01:06:09,799
I think this is tofu.

1743
01:06:10,167 --> 01:06:12,535
(Sian's on a roll,
trying yet another dish.)

1744
01:06:14,604 --> 01:06:15,537
It's good!

1745
01:06:16,072 --> 01:06:16,805
Tofu.

1746
01:06:16,806 --> 01:06:18,006
(Her foodie buddy grabs some right away.)

1747
01:06:18,441 --> 01:06:19,107
It's good, isn't it?

1748
01:06:19,108 --> 01:06:20,109
(Their tastes are in sync.)

1749
01:06:20,110 --> 01:06:21,944
- It's so good.
- A little like gochujang.

1750
01:06:21,945 --> 01:06:22,911
It's very Korean.

1751
01:06:23,180 --> 01:06:26,883
They all have this underlying flavor.

1752
01:06:27,150 --> 01:06:29,118
It's got this hint of...

1753
01:06:29,553 --> 01:06:31,520
Sichuan pepper throughout.

1754
01:06:32,489 --> 01:06:33,456
I absolutely love it.

1755
01:06:34,090 --> 01:06:35,023
(Haha)

1756
01:06:35,058 --> 01:06:36,558
I love it too.

1757
01:06:36,760 --> 01:06:38,260
Why's Indonesian food so good?

1758
01:06:39,029 --> 01:06:39,962
What's this?

1759
01:06:40,597 --> 01:06:41,497
Tofu?

1760
01:06:41,498 --> 01:06:43,065
(Meanwhile, Harimu tries a new dish.)

1761
01:06:43,934 --> 01:06:45,467
No way.

1762
01:06:45,735 --> 01:06:48,371
Potato croquette!

1763
01:06:49,172 --> 01:06:50,305
(Nom)

1764
01:06:50,306 --> 01:06:52,341
- Potato croquette.
- Sounds delicious.

1765
01:06:53,777 --> 01:06:55,244
Okay!

1766
01:06:56,713 --> 01:06:59,748
(Croquette feast begins.)

1767
01:07:00,083 --> 01:07:02,017
It's croquettes and nothing else for her.

1768
01:07:02,852 --> 01:07:04,553
(Gabee tries the croquettes too.)

1769
01:07:04,554 --> 01:07:06,355
- It's really salty.
- Which one?

1770
01:07:06,857 --> 01:07:09,425
- This.
- Yeah.

1771
01:07:11,061 --> 01:07:12,962
(Balance out the saltiness
with some shrimp chips.)

1772
01:07:12,963 --> 01:07:15,398
(Crunch)

1773
01:07:16,299 --> 01:07:17,799
It tastes so good
after being in the water.

1774
01:07:18,034 --> 01:07:18,900
Yeah.

1775
01:07:19,369 --> 01:07:20,502
It's so good.

1776
01:07:20,503 --> 01:07:21,370
(Nom)

1777
01:07:21,671 --> 01:07:25,874
(Digging into the jungle buffet.)

1778
01:07:26,176 --> 01:07:27,143
Honestly...

1779
01:07:27,878 --> 01:07:30,880
I didn't think
we'd get to feast like this.

1780
01:07:31,348 --> 01:07:33,549
I think we're all eating better here
than we do outside.

1781
01:07:33,550 --> 01:07:36,018
They even gave us snacks.

1782
01:07:36,220 --> 01:07:38,020
It's almost like a resort.

1783
01:07:38,889 --> 01:07:40,389
An all-inclusive.

1784
01:07:41,558 --> 01:07:43,926
The fire makes it smell like
we're out in the country.

1785
01:07:44,294 --> 01:07:45,161
(Thunder)

1786
01:07:45,162 --> 01:07:46,395
Whoa, thunder and lightning!

1787
01:07:46,730 --> 01:07:49,131
- Rumble!
- No way.

1788
01:07:49,132 --> 01:07:50,466
I think it's going to rain soon.

1789
01:07:50,467 --> 01:07:51,867
Why is there always lightning here?

1790
01:07:52,302 --> 01:07:53,068
I know, right?

1791
01:07:53,470 --> 01:07:55,303
Let's talk about...

1792
01:07:55,304 --> 01:07:56,571
our first impressions of each other.

1793
01:07:57,274 --> 01:07:58,574
- I like that.
- Oh, wow.

1794
01:07:58,575 --> 01:08:00,409
(There's always one person
who's into this stuff.)

1795
01:08:00,644 --> 01:08:02,345
I've known Gabee...

1796
01:08:02,879 --> 01:08:05,414
- for about 10 years.
- Oh, really?

1797
01:08:05,415 --> 01:08:08,551
- You were her student, right?
- Yes.

1798
01:08:08,552 --> 01:08:09,985
Being able to finally...

1799
01:08:09,986 --> 01:08:11,754
see her as an older sister on this trip...

1800
01:08:11,755 --> 01:08:14,022
means a lot to me.

1801
01:08:14,425 --> 01:08:16,826
It feels weird.
She's technically my teacher.

1802
01:08:16,827 --> 01:08:19,028
- Ms. Gabee!
- But I wanted us to be like sisters.

1803
01:08:19,362 --> 01:08:21,296
That's what I wanted on the first day.

1804
01:08:21,531 --> 01:08:24,032
But from day one,
she made me feel really comfortable.

1805
01:08:24,834 --> 01:08:26,668
She said, "It might feel awkward,
but just think of me as your big sister."

1806
01:08:26,669 --> 01:08:28,136
And I could tell she really meant it.

1807
01:08:28,338 --> 01:08:31,139
- You were touched.
- It was so sincere.

1808
01:08:31,241 --> 01:08:32,208
Yeah.

1809
01:08:32,209 --> 01:08:35,811
That's right. I thought you'd feel
a little uncomfortable.

1810
01:08:35,812 --> 01:08:37,346
I was so worried about that.

1811
01:08:37,347 --> 01:08:39,615
- Since you two are in the same field.
- Exactly.

1812
01:08:39,616 --> 01:08:41,783
- She's kind of senior.
- Of course.

1813
01:08:41,784 --> 01:08:43,152
And honestly,

1814
01:08:43,520 --> 01:08:45,422
I think the dance scene...

1815
01:08:45,423 --> 01:08:48,491
really needs someone like her.

1816
01:08:48,792 --> 01:08:50,459
I mean it.

1817
01:08:50,860 --> 01:08:52,160
I mean every word.

1818
01:08:52,328 --> 01:08:53,696
We need a dance star!

1819
01:08:54,130 --> 01:08:55,831
- Dance star.
- I mean it.

1820
01:08:55,832 --> 01:08:59,534
- We're going to be dance stars!
- Yes! Okay!

1821
01:08:59,535 --> 01:09:01,604
The next dance stars.

1822
01:09:01,605 --> 01:09:02,537
I'd seen Gabee...

1823
01:09:03,106 --> 01:09:05,541
plenty of times before.

1824
01:09:05,542 --> 01:09:07,976
- We met on "World Dice Tour" too.
- Yeah.

1825
01:09:08,178 --> 01:09:09,712
She's really thoughtful...

1826
01:09:10,380 --> 01:09:12,047
- and always looks out for people.
- So true.

1827
01:09:12,315 --> 01:09:14,516
I realized I hadn't been wrong
about her after all.

1828
01:09:14,752 --> 01:09:16,418
That's our queen Gabee!

1829
01:09:16,419 --> 01:09:17,453
(Laughing)

1830
01:09:17,754 --> 01:09:20,823
You really sound like a true fan!

1831
01:09:21,124 --> 01:09:22,224
That's our queen!

1832
01:09:23,626 --> 01:09:26,161
As for Sian...

1833
01:09:26,563 --> 01:09:29,832
At first, I wasn't sure if Sian
and I would really get along.

1834
01:09:30,100 --> 01:09:31,467
Oh, why?

1835
01:09:31,468 --> 01:09:34,103
Because...

1836
01:09:34,104 --> 01:09:37,206
I'd seen her clash with some
of the girls on "Single's Inferno."

1837
01:09:37,841 --> 01:09:39,475
(She thought Sian was a total ice queen.)

1838
01:09:39,476 --> 01:09:41,777
- Darn!
- But!

1839
01:09:41,845 --> 01:09:42,912
She was like, "Gabee!"

1840
01:09:42,913 --> 01:09:44,880
Yeah.

1841
01:09:44,881 --> 01:09:46,615
Was I like this?

1842
01:09:46,616 --> 01:09:47,650
That's the vibe she gave me.

1843
01:09:47,651 --> 01:09:50,052
She was totally giving
little sister vibes.

1844
01:09:50,053 --> 01:09:50,953
Yeah.

1845
01:09:50,954 --> 01:09:51,821
And she's so nice.

1846
01:09:52,790 --> 01:09:53,889
(Blushing)

1847
01:09:54,190 --> 01:09:55,023
So nice.

1848
01:09:55,191 --> 01:09:58,026
And Sian was the last one to arrive.

1849
01:09:58,027 --> 01:09:58,827
The last one.

1850
01:09:58,828 --> 01:10:00,228
Like the wildcard.

1851
01:10:00,229 --> 01:10:02,264
- A wildcard.
- When I saw her...

1852
01:10:02,265 --> 01:10:04,567
I was like,
"Who's that gorgeous silhouette?"

1853
01:10:04,568 --> 01:10:06,001
Exactly.

1854
01:10:06,069 --> 01:10:08,871
So these two were like,
"Is she an actress?"

1855
01:10:08,872 --> 01:10:09,872
Really?

1856
01:10:09,873 --> 01:10:12,207
Then I recognized you as you got closer.

1857
01:10:12,208 --> 01:10:13,242
(Kyaaa!)

1858
01:10:13,243 --> 01:10:17,813
I felt like I could really lean on you.

1859
01:10:17,814 --> 01:10:19,348
- Right away.
- Really?

1860
01:10:19,749 --> 01:10:21,049
So, were you able to?

1861
01:10:21,050 --> 01:10:22,818
Yeah, totally!

1862
01:10:22,919 --> 01:10:24,820
May seem aloof,
but actually a total softie.

1863
01:10:24,821 --> 01:10:25,921
(Sian's actually such a sweetheart.)

1864
01:10:26,055 --> 01:10:27,989
I saw you on YouTube.

1865
01:10:28,291 --> 01:10:31,059
You're such a strong, determined person.

1866
01:10:31,227 --> 01:10:32,694
You made me realize successful people...

1867
01:10:32,695 --> 01:10:35,097
- really do have that inner strength.
- I thought that too.

1868
01:10:35,098 --> 01:10:37,133
You're so responsible.

1869
01:10:37,134 --> 01:10:39,668
- You really come off as a strong woman.
- Yeah.

1870
01:10:40,003 --> 01:10:41,704
A cute voice.

1871
01:10:41,705 --> 01:10:42,938
But a strong core.

1872
01:10:43,673 --> 01:10:44,473
(Strong)

1873
01:10:44,474 --> 01:10:46,141
- Meow.
- That's what that is.

1874
01:10:46,142 --> 01:10:48,176
When I told people
I was doing a show like this,

1875
01:10:48,411 --> 01:10:50,178
they all said,

1876
01:10:50,413 --> 01:10:52,548
"I hope Won Ji's on it."

1877
01:10:52,549 --> 01:10:53,949
"Please become friends with her!"

1878
01:10:53,950 --> 01:10:55,884
"Please!"

1879
01:10:55,885 --> 01:10:57,986
And you were actually there.

1880
01:10:57,987 --> 01:10:59,087
But you seemed a little...

1881
01:10:59,390 --> 01:11:00,255
startled.

1882
01:11:00,257 --> 01:11:02,191
- You were a little taken aback.
- Yeah.

1883
01:11:02,192 --> 01:11:04,327
- "Oh..."
- "What kind of combination is this?"

1884
01:11:04,328 --> 01:11:06,128
Yeah.
I could feel her.

1885
01:11:06,129 --> 01:11:08,297
A little surprised.

1886
01:11:08,298 --> 01:11:11,400
So I decided to approach her slowly.

1887
01:11:11,401 --> 01:11:13,969
See? She's really quick
at figuring people out.

1888
01:11:13,970 --> 01:11:16,272
That's what I thought.

1889
01:11:16,273 --> 01:11:18,540
But I feel like we really click.

1890
01:11:18,541 --> 01:11:20,842
I could totally brag about it
to my friends.

1891
01:11:20,843 --> 01:11:22,912
"We're basically besties now!"

1892
01:11:22,913 --> 01:11:24,213
- Jealous?
- Besties!

1893
01:11:24,214 --> 01:11:26,682
I think I could brag like this
when I go back.

1894
01:11:26,683 --> 01:11:27,850
You're so much fun.

1895
01:11:27,850 --> 01:11:30,499
I had only seen Harimu through Reels.

1896
01:11:30,500 --> 01:11:31,700
I'm honored.

1897
01:11:31,804 --> 01:11:33,610
I honestly thought she was a foreigner.

1898
01:11:34,230 --> 01:11:36,204
That's the best compliment.

1899
01:11:36,205 --> 01:11:38,440
- I thought you were a foreigner.
- That can happen.

1900
01:11:38,683 --> 01:11:40,475
I only knew Harimu...

1901
01:11:40,742 --> 01:11:42,444
from a distance.

1902
01:11:42,730 --> 01:11:47,015
We never really had time to get close
or get to know her personality.

1903
01:11:47,382 --> 01:11:49,284
But it turns out she is
such a great person.

1904
01:11:50,385 --> 01:11:54,589
It made me wonder why I
never took the time to get to know her.

1905
01:11:54,590 --> 01:11:55,794
I wish I had.

1906
01:11:55,795 --> 01:11:57,074
That really is a compliment.

1907
01:11:57,075 --> 01:11:59,328
It's not like I had a bad impression
of you before, but...

1908
01:11:59,749 --> 01:12:03,498
I don't really...

1909
01:12:03,535 --> 01:12:05,474
- Show your personality, right?
- Exactly.

1910
01:12:05,475 --> 01:12:06,335
I noticed.

1911
01:12:06,336 --> 01:12:09,004
I like getting to know someone
naturally over time.

1912
01:12:09,015 --> 01:12:11,215
I like meeting people naturally.

1913
01:12:11,216 --> 01:12:13,408
I strongly prefer
meeting people naturally.

1914
01:12:13,409 --> 01:12:15,143
(That's why she kept insisting
on "meeting naturally.")

1915
01:12:15,223 --> 01:12:17,646
She seemed like a purely cheerful person.

1916
01:12:17,776 --> 01:12:21,049
But I think she actually has
a lot of depth.

1917
01:12:22,709 --> 01:12:25,954
She's perceptive and capable too.

1918
01:12:26,421 --> 01:12:28,223
I highly recommend Harimu.

1919
01:12:28,815 --> 01:12:29,858
"Highly recommend?"

1920
01:12:30,726 --> 01:12:32,962
(Harimu, the youngest,
is the sisters' top pick.)

1921
01:12:33,055 --> 01:12:35,197
Would you come back
to the jungle for another trip?

1922
01:12:35,233 --> 01:12:36,832
Maybe once?

1923
01:12:36,853 --> 01:12:37,933
Once?

1924
01:12:38,080 --> 01:12:41,002
I think it'd be nice
to come with friends or family.

1925
01:12:41,820 --> 01:12:45,307
- It's a great place to actually talk.
- Exactly. People you can talk to...

1926
01:12:45,700 --> 01:12:47,142
Here's the thing.

1927
01:12:47,324 --> 01:12:49,745
Holding a "Divorce Re-Boot Camp" here.

1928
01:12:49,804 --> 01:12:50,979
That's...

1929
01:12:51,747 --> 01:12:53,215
That'd be chaos.

1930
01:12:53,815 --> 01:12:54,850
That'd be fun.

1931
01:12:54,858 --> 01:12:57,986
I think it'd also be good
for couples before marriage.

1932
01:12:58,022 --> 01:12:59,855
They could get to know
each other's personalities.

1933
01:13:00,021 --> 01:13:01,123
That'd be fun.

1934
01:13:01,124 --> 01:13:04,524
(Bukit Lawang is the perfect place
for those with big decisions to make.)

1935
01:13:04,549 --> 01:13:06,549
I want to go to the Amazon...

1936
01:13:07,195 --> 01:13:09,364
as my team is called AMAZON.

1937
01:13:09,393 --> 01:13:11,700
- True.
- I have to live up to the name.

1938
01:13:11,833 --> 01:13:14,660
I want to go there
with them at least once.

1939
01:13:14,661 --> 01:13:17,672
A mental-strength training workshop.

1940
01:13:17,760 --> 01:13:18,640
Totally.

1941
01:13:18,667 --> 01:13:20,742
Like I said earlier,

1942
01:13:21,143 --> 01:13:25,781
I never really challenged my limits.

1943
01:13:26,291 --> 01:13:30,252
I tended to always avoid them.

1944
01:13:30,691 --> 01:13:32,911
But hiking mountains,

1945
01:13:32,951 --> 01:13:34,556
going into the jungle,

1946
01:13:34,918 --> 01:13:36,792
and feeding elephants...

1947
01:13:36,793 --> 01:13:38,892
made me feel like
I had pushed past my limits.

1948
01:13:38,981 --> 01:13:42,164
So I learned and felt
so much from this trip.

1949
01:13:42,908 --> 01:13:43,899
For me,

1950
01:13:44,499 --> 01:13:46,601
I had been doubting...

1951
01:13:47,502 --> 01:13:49,771
some of my abilities.

1952
01:13:49,819 --> 01:13:51,206
- Why?
- How come?

1953
01:13:51,231 --> 01:13:52,340
(Surprised)

1954
01:13:52,466 --> 01:13:56,645
I was wondering if I was
actually a worthwhile person.

1955
01:13:57,712 --> 01:14:01,917
Then Won Ji told me I was
smart for the first time in my life.

1956
01:14:02,317 --> 01:14:04,317
You gave me so many compliments,

1957
01:14:04,350 --> 01:14:07,689
and it made me
feel like I was actually useful.

1958
01:14:08,504 --> 01:14:10,025
You're totally...

1959
01:14:10,295 --> 01:14:12,687
I really liked that about this trip.

1960
01:14:12,688 --> 01:14:15,664
Feeling like I'm valuable somewhere.

1961
01:14:16,798 --> 01:14:21,269
I usually travel a lot,

1962
01:14:21,512 --> 01:14:24,072
so I thought I was already
pretty good at packing light.

1963
01:14:24,752 --> 01:14:29,044
But I think I've learned how to get
rid of even more unnecessary baggage.

1964
01:14:29,678 --> 01:14:32,030
Was there nothing good
about spending time with us?

1965
01:14:32,934 --> 01:14:34,683
- What about us?
- What about me?

1966
01:14:34,703 --> 01:14:36,654
(The younger sisters want
to hear something from their eldest.)

1967
01:14:36,848 --> 01:14:38,920
(Gathering around)

1968
01:14:39,039 --> 01:14:41,639
I think I relied on Won Ji every moment.

1969
01:14:41,640 --> 01:14:42,657
Really?

1970
01:14:42,966 --> 01:14:47,304
Whether we were bargaining,
going somewhere, or buying something,

1971
01:14:47,305 --> 01:14:49,698
I relied on you a lot.

1972
01:14:49,726 --> 01:14:51,933
But that might have been a burden for you.

1973
01:14:51,934 --> 01:14:54,302
Yes, I think it was probably a lot.

1974
01:14:54,625 --> 01:14:56,238
I'm totally fine with that.

1975
01:14:57,211 --> 01:14:59,708
It's what I always do anyway.

1976
01:14:59,885 --> 01:15:02,811
As the oldest one in this group,

1977
01:15:03,578 --> 01:15:06,047
the trip is...

1978
01:15:06,142 --> 01:15:07,082
Are you crying?

1979
01:15:08,902 --> 01:15:10,752
- Seriously?
- Are you?

1980
01:15:14,990 --> 01:15:17,392
To be honest...

1981
01:15:21,763 --> 01:15:24,074
But you must have had such a hard time.

1982
01:15:24,075 --> 01:15:25,233
It's not that.

1983
01:15:25,234 --> 01:15:26,981
(Overwhelmed with emotion)

1984
01:15:27,742 --> 01:15:29,094
Was it really that hard?

1985
01:15:29,095 --> 01:15:31,273
It's not that it was hard.

1986
01:15:31,640 --> 01:15:32,774
I'm actually...

1987
01:15:33,408 --> 01:15:35,031
not very good at being a leader.

1988
01:15:35,055 --> 01:15:37,212
I'm never that kind of person.

1989
01:15:37,846 --> 01:15:41,068
(A moment caught
between wanting to lead the trip well,)

1990
01:15:41,158 --> 01:15:42,447
But...

1991
01:15:42,566 --> 01:15:44,899
(and doubting herself as the oldest.)

1992
01:15:45,059 --> 01:15:47,756
But I learned so much from you.

1993
01:15:48,070 --> 01:15:49,824
You're totally a natural leader.

1994
01:15:49,863 --> 01:15:51,526
You're a hardcore leader.

1995
01:15:52,103 --> 01:15:53,795
You're the ultimate leader.

1996
01:15:54,428 --> 01:15:55,676
You're at max leader level.

1997
01:15:55,700 --> 01:15:56,818
(Thank you.)

1998
01:15:57,071 --> 01:16:00,168
(The extroverted younger sisters'
way of comforting her.)

1999
01:16:00,331 --> 01:16:02,837
- It really weighed on you, right?
- I think so.

2000
01:16:02,858 --> 01:16:05,890
But she really did work hard.

2001
01:16:05,924 --> 01:16:08,476
With four people, it's a group.

2002
01:16:09,210 --> 01:16:11,513
So you probably felt
a lot of responsibility.

2003
01:16:11,617 --> 01:16:16,217
And it was our first trip
with all four of us.

2004
01:16:16,785 --> 01:16:19,120
It must've been awkward
and difficult at times.

2005
01:16:19,421 --> 01:16:22,029
But I think we each did
our part really well.

2006
01:16:22,054 --> 01:16:23,725
- Absolutely.
- That's right.

2007
01:16:24,018 --> 01:16:26,094
I'm glad there were four of us.

2008
01:16:26,488 --> 01:16:28,740
(Tight hug)

2009
01:16:28,760 --> 01:16:29,965
I love the four of us.

2010
01:16:31,226 --> 01:16:33,802
- We each have our own role.
- Absolutely.

2011
01:16:34,613 --> 01:16:36,004
It's getting hot now.

2012
01:16:37,915 --> 01:16:40,475
(The four have grown even closer.)

2013
01:16:41,309 --> 01:16:43,812
So we just have to go home
tomorrow, right?

2014
01:16:43,813 --> 01:16:45,501
(An awkward feeling suddenly settles in.)

2015
01:16:45,526 --> 01:16:46,815
We've finished eating.

2016
01:16:47,248 --> 01:16:48,817
Let's talk, play, and then sleep.

2017
01:16:48,818 --> 01:16:50,318
- Sounds good.
- Bedtime.

2018
01:16:50,393 --> 01:16:52,954
- It's really dark there.
- We shouldn't look out there.

2019
01:16:53,126 --> 01:16:55,579
It's really scary there.

2020
01:16:55,580 --> 01:16:57,492
Let's use the bathroom before bed.

2021
01:16:57,546 --> 01:16:59,694
It was a good time.

2022
01:16:59,859 --> 01:17:01,129
It's really scary.

2023
01:17:01,579 --> 01:17:03,872
- Do you think you can sleep, Harimu?
- No.

2024
01:17:03,873 --> 01:17:07,039
(After spending an even more
bonding night together)

2025
01:17:09,046 --> 01:17:11,719
(The older ones go and shower first.)

2026
01:17:12,039 --> 01:17:14,409
We have to take care
of ourselves even in the jungle.

2027
01:17:14,410 --> 01:17:15,510
Of course we do.

2028
01:17:15,699 --> 01:17:18,148
(Sian and Harimu begin
their nighttime skincare routine.)

2029
01:17:18,173 --> 01:17:22,117
We need to soothe our skin, especially
after a long day of skin irritation.

2030
01:17:22,417 --> 01:17:24,719
This doesn't feel sticky at all,

2031
01:17:25,153 --> 01:17:27,722
- and it moisturizes really well.
- I know.

2032
01:17:27,995 --> 01:17:30,458
You know how your sleep quality is better,

2033
01:17:30,688 --> 01:17:33,628
- when your skincare routine is perfect?
- Exactly.

2034
01:17:33,629 --> 01:17:37,699
You have to seal everything
in with a layer of skincare.

2035
01:17:38,082 --> 01:17:40,335
We're in the jungle right now.

2036
01:17:40,582 --> 01:17:41,603
Can you believe this?

2037
01:17:43,405 --> 01:17:45,139
Does the jungle make
our skin more hydrated?

2038
01:17:45,942 --> 01:17:48,877
Anyway, we survived.

2039
01:17:48,878 --> 01:17:51,813
We survived even the jungle.

2040
01:17:52,735 --> 01:17:54,883
- Let's go straight to bed.
- Okay.

2041
01:17:55,450 --> 01:17:57,450
And that was our
nighttime skincare routine.

2042
01:17:58,006 --> 01:18:01,690
(Sian carries her through
getting ready for bed.)

2043
01:18:02,313 --> 01:18:05,260
(After finishing their nighttime skincare,
it's finally time to sleep.)

2044
01:18:05,746 --> 01:18:08,724
(Inside the accommodation)

2045
01:18:08,991 --> 01:18:11,611
(Gabee is the first one to come in.)

2046
01:18:12,497 --> 01:18:14,769
- Let me know if you need any medicine.
- Okay.

2047
01:18:16,017 --> 01:18:17,005
(Gabee is already asleep.)

2048
01:18:17,022 --> 01:18:18,306
(Sian is also all ready for bed.)

2049
01:18:18,989 --> 01:18:22,649
(She slips into the bed beside Gabee.)

2050
01:18:25,075 --> 01:18:28,722
(Won Ji and Harimu return
from the bathroom.)

2051
01:18:28,928 --> 01:18:30,118
They're already out cold.

2052
01:18:30,835 --> 01:18:32,802
(Looking around)

2053
01:18:33,975 --> 01:18:38,886
(She fixes the mosquito nets
over Gabee and Sian.)

2054
01:18:39,600 --> 01:18:42,300
(Then gets into bed.)

2055
01:18:42,620 --> 01:18:45,266
This isn't really doing anything.

2056
01:18:45,866 --> 01:18:48,364
(Won Ji's mosquito net
seems a little off.)

2057
01:18:48,871 --> 01:18:51,258
(She just lies down.)

2058
01:18:51,458 --> 01:18:52,807
Not bad.

2059
01:18:53,608 --> 01:18:56,111
If you need to go to the bathroom,

2060
01:18:58,179 --> 01:19:00,315
just tell me.

2061
01:19:00,541 --> 01:19:02,617
That would be too rude.

2062
01:19:02,775 --> 01:19:03,818
No.

2063
01:19:04,619 --> 01:19:08,056
Then let's just agree
to do it for each other.

2064
01:19:09,867 --> 01:19:11,267
(Rustling)

2065
01:19:11,973 --> 01:19:14,406
I really can't see anything.

2066
01:19:14,407 --> 01:19:18,600
(The end of Night 7 in the jungle)

2067
01:19:20,965 --> 01:19:23,274
Harimu and I came up with a dance.

2068
01:19:23,638 --> 01:19:25,708
(Learning the Abra-ca-Empty choreography)

2069
01:19:27,294 --> 01:19:28,841
(The center with standout dance line)

2070
01:19:29,167 --> 01:19:30,394
(What's this?)

2071
01:19:30,634 --> 01:19:31,788
I got it.

2072
01:19:32,034 --> 01:19:32,954
No, you didn't.

2073
01:19:33,248 --> 01:19:34,961
You didn't. I saw everything.

2074
01:19:35,227 --> 01:19:36,708
She seems a little bossy.

2075
01:19:36,834 --> 01:19:38,174
She says you're too bossy.

2076
01:19:38,568 --> 01:19:42,306
(A special training session
just for Won Ji.)

2077
01:19:43,352 --> 01:19:45,606
(The rookie monster's
performance coming soon)

2078
01:19:46,146 --> 01:19:47,679
(Check-out day at the jungle camp)

2079
01:19:47,906 --> 01:19:49,719
Did you wash your face
and brush your teeth?

2080
01:19:49,971 --> 01:19:50,512
No, I didn't.

2081
01:19:50,819 --> 01:19:52,517
(The four have grown
much closer overnight.)

2082
01:19:52,837 --> 01:19:54,057
We're taking a taxi down.

2083
01:19:54,330 --> 01:19:56,230
(A jungle taxi made of connected tubes)

2084
01:19:56,790 --> 01:19:59,017
(Back to civilization
on the garlic-bread tube)

2085
01:19:59,313 --> 01:20:00,844
That's our first obstacle.

2086
01:20:01,050 --> 01:20:02,370
Ten seconds to launch.

2087
01:20:02,604 --> 01:20:04,255
Here we go.

2088
01:20:04,846 --> 01:20:06,921
(Wobble)

2089
01:20:07,281 --> 01:20:09,407
I'm completely soaked.
Even my underwear is soaked.

2090
01:20:10,235 --> 01:20:11,019
Ipu.

2091
01:20:13,275 --> 01:20:14,535
(Whoosh)

2092
01:20:14,861 --> 01:20:15,861
Are you okay, Ipu?

2093
01:20:18,621 --> 01:20:20,428
(Serious)

2094
01:20:20,829 --> 01:20:23,548
(An unexpected situation arises.)

2095
01:20:23,549 --> 01:20:25,054
(Is something wrong with the tube?)

2096
01:20:25,055 --> 01:20:26,182
Why is he serious again?

2097
01:20:26,601 --> 01:20:28,795
(Will they make it safely
out of the jungle?)

2098
01:20:30,215 --> 01:20:31,988
Are you okay, Harimu?

2099
01:20:31,989 --> 01:20:33,881
- You're still not feeling well, are you?
- No.

2100
01:20:33,882 --> 01:20:35,782
- Oh, no.
- Let me see.

2101
01:20:36,576 --> 01:20:39,209
She has a really high fever.
What do we do?

2102
01:20:39,796 --> 01:20:42,517
(In the end, filming is halted
and she is taken to the hospital.)

2103
01:20:43,087 --> 01:20:45,673
(Harimu developed
a high fever and abdominal pain.)

2104
01:20:46,567 --> 01:20:49,313
(It's an unfamiliar sight
from someone normally so full of energy.)

2105
01:20:49,980 --> 01:20:52,087
(What on earth happened to her?)

2106
01:20:53,223 --> 01:20:55,163
Dramaday.me
